{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:01:32", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f992029f-b922-4c2b-82e4-a2d5ae6ff1a7', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Frontend Components Development - Create React components for the Project View Dashboard",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0185Vxmz8JrrmhGecvAVXo7r', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0185Vxmz8JrrmhGecvAVXo7r', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent Backend Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Core Design Philosophy\\n- Modular, event-driven backend architecture\\n- High observability and resilience\\n- Minimal performance overhead\\n- Seamless error recovery\\n\\n### High-Level Architecture Pattern\\n- Event-Driven Microservices\\n- CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) for metrics and state management\\n- Pub/Sub for real-time progress streaming\\n\\n## 2. Technology Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+ (type hints, asyncio)\\n- **Async Framework**: `asyncio` + `uvloop` for high-performance concurrency\\n- **WebSocket**: `websockets` library\\n- **Event Bus**: `aio-pika` (AMQP-based message queue)\\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + `prometheus_client`\\n- **Persistence**: SQLAlchemy with PostgreSQL\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- Python chosen for its strong async capabilities and rich AI/ML ecosystem\\n- `asyncio` provides efficient concurrent execution without heavy threading\\n- Prometheus offers robust metrics collection with minimal overhead\\n- PostgreSQL ensures strong consistency for state persistence\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### 1. AgentRuntime (Enhanced)\\n- Responsible for agent lifecycle management\\n- Emits granular progress events\\n- Handles automatic error recovery\\n- Coordinates state checkpointing\\n\\n### 2. StateManager\\n- Manages agent state persistence\\n- Implements checkpoint/resume functionality\\n- Supports partial state reconstruction\\n- Handles context preservation during retries\\n\\n### 3. ProgressEventBus\\n- Centralized event streaming mechanism\\n- Publishes real-time agent progress\\n- Supports WebSocket broadcasting\\n- Low-latency event routing\\n\\n### 4. AgentAnalytics\\n- Collects performance metrics\\n- Tracks token usage, success rates\\n- Provides adaptive model selection logic\\n- Generates performance reports\\n\\n### 5. ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Classifies errors (retriable vs fatal)\\n- Manages retry strategies\\n- Implements exponential backoff\\n- Tracks error history for optimization\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\nAgent Spawn Request\\n    \\u2193\\n[AgentRuntime]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Start Execution\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Emit Progress Events \\u2192 [ProgressEventBus]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Checkpoint State \\u2192 [StateManager]\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Track Metrics \\u2192 [AgentAnalytics]\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 On Error \\u2192 [ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator]\\n        \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Retry Logic\\n        \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 State Resume\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Performance Tracking\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Token Usage\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Success Rates\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Model Performance\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Key Implementation Details\\n\\n### Progress Streaming\\n- Use WebSocket for real-time updates\\n- Event types:\\n  - `agent_spawn`\\n  - `tool_invocation_start`\\n  - `tool_invocation_complete`\\n  - `agent_state_change`\\n  - `error_occurred`\\n\\n### Error Recovery Strategy\\n- Checkpoint every significant state transition\\n- Store:\\n  - Conversation history\\n  - Tool execution results\\n  - Spawned agent context\\n- Retry mechanism:\\n  1. Exponential backoff\\n  2. Maximum retry limit\\n  3. Fallback to manual intervention\\n\\n### Analytics Collection\\n- Metrics per agent:\\n  - Execution time\\n  - Token consumption\\n  - Success/failure rate\\n  - Model tier performance\\n- Aggregation levels:\\n  - Per agent instance\\n  - Per agent type\\n  - Across system\\n\\n## 6. Deployment Considerations\\n\\n### Container Strategy\\n- Docker containers for each component\\n- Docker Compose for local development\\n- Kubernetes for production scaling\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n- Use `.env` files for configuration\\n- Support multiple environments:\\n  - Development\\n  - Staging\\n  - Production\\n\\n## 7. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Testing Approaches\\n- Unit Tests: `pytest`\\n- Integration Tests: `pytest-asyncio`\\n- Performance Tests: `locust`\\n- Coverage: `coverage.py`\\n\\n### Test Coverage Requirements\\n- 90%+ unit test coverage\\n- Integration tests for error recovery\\n- Chaos testing for resilience verification\\n\\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. Performance Overhead from Metrics\\n   - **Mitigation**: Sampling, async metrics collection\\n2. WebSocket Connection Instability\\n   - **Mitigation**: Reconnection logic, connection pooling\\n3. State Persistence Complexity\\n   - **Mitigation**: Robust serialization, comprehensive testing\\n\\n## 9. Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. Preferred message queue technology (current proposal: AMQP)\\n2. Specific performance budget for metrics collection\\n3. Desired granularity of progress events\\n\\n## 10. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Synchronous Execution\\n- **Pros**: Simpler implementation\\n- **Cons**: Poor concurrency, blocking operations\\n- **Verdict**: Rejected in favor of async design\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Separate Metrics Service\\n- **Pros**: Clearer separation of concerns\\n- **Cons**: Additional complexity, network overhead\\n- **Verdict**: Current design integrated for performance\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, performant backend for the ensemble agent system, focusing on real-time visibility, error resilience, and continuous improvement through comprehensive analytics."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014zN4UE7ymJ9ygr2q7L5Mez', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014zN4UE7ymJ9ygr2q7L5Mez', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard Requirements\\n\\n## Overview\\nAdd a dedicated Project View to the Ensemble UI that provides comprehensive visibility into a project\'s status, SDLC position, milestone progress, and next steps with actionable controls.\\n\\n## User Vision\\n\\"Let\'s add a project view, so we can see a project view, its status, its position in the SDLC, the number of milestones determined, the number completed, and next steps along with a \'continue to next step\' button to force the agent system to move to implementation.\\"\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Goals\\n1. **Project Status Visibility**: Display comprehensive project status at a glance\\n2. **SDLC Position Tracking**: Show where the project is in the Software Development Lifecycle\\n3. **Milestone Progress**: Display milestone counts (total, completed, remaining)\\n4. **Next Steps Visibility**: Show actionable next steps for the project\\n5. **Manual Control**: Provide \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button to force advancement\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n- Users can view project status without navigating multiple screens\\n- SDLC phase is clearly visible (requirements \\u2192 architecture \\u2192 planning \\u2192 implementation \\u2192 testing \\u2192 complete)\\n- Milestone progress shows as numerical count and visual progress indicator\\n- Next steps are clearly listed with descriptions\\n- \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button triggers agent system to advance implementation\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR-1: Project Selection\\n- Display list of active projects (from `/api/projects/summary` or project tracker)\\n- Allow selection of a specific project to view details\\n- Show project name, created date, and current status in list\\n\\n### FR-2: Project Status Display\\n- Show overall project status: active, paused, completed, failed\\n- Display project name and description\\n- Show creation timestamp and last update timestamp\\n- Display associated request_id for tracing\\n\\n### FR-3: SDLC Position Indicator\\n- Visual indicator showing current phase:\\n  - Requirements\\n  - Architecture\\n  - Planning (task breakdown)\\n  - Implementation\\n  - Testing\\n  - Complete\\n- Phase should be determined from project tracking data or Executive Director output\\n\\n### FR-4: Milestone Tracking\\n- Display total number of milestones determined\\n- Show number of milestones completed\\n- Show number of milestones remaining/in-progress\\n- Visual progress bar (completed/total)\\n- List individual milestones with their status\\n\\n### FR-5: Task Summary\\n- Show task counts by status (todo, in_progress, completed, blocked)\\n- Completion percentage\\n- Link to detailed task view if available\\n\\n### FR-6: Next Steps Display\\n- List next actionable steps for the project\\n- Show which tasks can be started (no blocking dependencies)\\n- Display agent assignments for pending tasks\\n\\n### FR-7: Continue to Next Step Button\\n- Button to trigger continuation of project execution\\n- When clicked:\\n  - Spawn a new Executive Director with context to continue\\n  - Pass project_id and current state\\n  - Include instruction to proceed to next phase/milestone\\n- Visual feedback during execution (loading state)\\n- Error handling for failed continuations\\n\\n### FR-8: Agent Activity for Project\\n- Show currently running agents for this project\\n- Display recent agent activity\\n- Link to agent hierarchy for the project\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Backend Integration\\n\\n#### Existing Endpoints to Leverage\\n- `GET /api/projects/summary` - List projects with summary stats\\n- `GET /api/activity/hierarchy` - Agent hierarchy for project\\n- `GET /api/requests/{request_id}/timeline` - Timeline data\\n- `POST /api/generate-solution` - For continuation functionality\\n\\n#### New/Enhanced Endpoints Needed\\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/details` - Detailed project view with milestones\\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Trigger project continuation\\n\\n### Data Sources\\n- Project Tracker (`~/.ensemble/projects/`) - SDLC state, milestones, notes\\n- Swarm State (SQLite) - Active agents, session data\\n- Activity Tracker - Recent activities\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n- New view tab \\"Projects\\" in App.jsx navigation\\n- ProjectView.jsx - Main component\\n- ProjectStatusCard.jsx - Project header with status\\n- SDLCIndicator.jsx - Visual SDLC phase indicator\\n- MilestoneProgress.jsx - Milestone tracking display\\n- NextStepsPanel.jsx - Actionable next steps\\n\\n## UI/UX Specifications\\n\\n### Visual Design\\n- Follow existing dark theme (backgroundColor: \'#1a1d29\')\\n- Card-based layout consistent with other views\\n- Use existing Badge component for status indicators\\n- Progress bars for milestone completion\\n\\n### Layout (Desktop)\\n```\\n+--------------------------------------------------+\\n| [Navigation: Activity | Timeline | ... | Projects] |\\n+--------------------------------------------------+\\n| Project List (Left)  |  Project Details (Right)   |\\n|                      |                            |\\n| [Project 1]         | Project Name                |\\n| [Project 2] <--     | Status: Active | Phase: X   |\\n| [Project 3]         |                            |\\n|                     | SDLC Progress              |\\n|                     | [=====>------] Architecture |\\n|                     |                            |\\n|                     | Milestones                 |\\n|                     | 3/7 Complete [=====>--]    |\\n|                     |                            |\\n|                     | Next Steps                 |\\n|                     | \\u2022 Task A (assigned: Dev)   |\\n|                     | \\u2022 Task B (unassigned)      |\\n|                     |                            |\\n|                     | [Continue to Next Step]    |\\n+--------------------------------------------------+\\n```\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Project list should load in < 500ms\\n- Project details should load in < 1s\\n- Continue action should show immediate feedback\\n\\n### Reliability\\n- Handle missing/incomplete project data gracefully\\n- Show meaningful error states\\n- Recover from backend failures\\n\\n### Accessibility\\n- Keyboard navigation for project selection\\n- Screen reader compatible status indicators\\n- Clear visual contrast for all states\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Project deletion/archival (future feature)\\n- Milestone editing (manual intervention)\\n- Budget/cost per project (exists in Cost Tracking view)\\n- Multi-project comparison view\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing project_tracker.py module\\n- Backend main.py endpoints\\n- React Bootstrap UI framework\\n- Existing API service layer\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n1. Project data is available in ~/.ensemble/projects/ directory\\n2. Executive Director agents create and maintain project state\\n3. SDLC phase is tracked in project notes or result status\\n4. Backend has access to project tracker module\\n\\n## Risks\\n- SDLC phase may not be consistently tracked in current implementation\\n- Milestone data may be sparse for older projects\\n- \\"Continue\\" action may require careful context preservation\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015GUvRtrQnPoBTGmGVYKmaF', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Frontend Tasks - Project View Dashboard\\n\\n## Overview\\nBreakdown of React component development tasks for the Project View Dashboard feature.\\n\\n## Task Dependencies\\nTasks are organized in dependency order - components without dependencies should be built first.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Core UI Components (No Dependencies)\\n\\n### Task 1: Badge Component Enhancement\\n**Description**: Enhance existing Badge component to support status variants for project phases\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Badge supports SDLC phase variants (requirements, architecture, planning, implementation, testing, complete)\\n- Badge supports project status variants (active, paused, completed, failed, error)\\n- Proper color coding for each status type\\n- Consistent with existing dark theme\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n**Files**: `Badge.jsx` (enhancement)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 2: Progress Bar Component\\n**Description**: Create reusable ProgressBar component for milestone progress visualization\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Visual progress bar with percentage completion\\n- Shows completed/total as text overlay\\n- Dark theme compatible colors\\n- Supports different sizes (small, medium, large)\\n- Optional animated fill transition\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n**Files**: `components/ProgressBar.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 3: SDLC Indicator Component\\n**Description**: Create visual indicator for Software Development Lifecycle phases\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Horizontal stepper showing 6 phases: Requirements → Architecture → Planning → Implementation → Testing → Complete\\n- Highlights current phase\\n- Shows completed phases as checked\\n- Responsive design for mobile\\n- Hover tooltips for phase descriptions\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Badge component\\n**Files**: `components/SDLCIndicator.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 4: Project Status Card Component\\n**Description**: Card component displaying project header information and status\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Shows project name, description, and timestamps\\n- Displays current status with Badge component\\n- Shows current SDLC phase with indicator\\n- Loading state support\\n- Error state display\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Badge, SDLCIndicator\\n**Files**: `components/ProjectStatusCard.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 5: Milestone Progress Component\\n**Description**: Component displaying milestone tracking information\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Shows milestone counts (completed/total)\\n- Visual progress bar for completion percentage\\n- List of individual milestones with status badges\\n- Expandable/collapsible milestone list\\n- Empty state when no milestones exist\\n\\n**Dependencies**: ProgressBar, Badge\\n**Files**: `components/MilestoneProgress.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 6: Next Steps Panel Component\\n**Description**: Panel showing actionable next steps and tasks\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Lists next actionable steps with descriptions\\n- Shows task assignments and status\\n- Prioritizes unblocked tasks\\n- Shows task dependencies if applicable\\n- Empty state when no next steps available\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Badge\\n**Files**: `components/NextStepsPanel.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 7: Project List Component\\n**Description**: Sidebar component listing all projects with selection capability\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Displays project names with status indicators\\n- Shows last updated timestamp\\n- Supports project selection (single select)\\n- Search/filter functionality\\n- Loading and error states\\n- Responsive collapsible on mobile\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Badge\\n**Files**: `components/ProjectList.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Main Page Components\\n\\n### Task 8: Project Details Panel Component\\n**Description**: Main content area showing detailed project information\\n**Complexity**: Complex\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Integrates ProjectStatusCard, SDLCIndicator, MilestoneProgress, and NextStepsPanel\\n- Handles data loading from API\\n- Error handling for missing/incomplete project data\\n- \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button with loading states\\n- Responsive layout for mobile devices\\n\\n**Dependencies**: ProjectStatusCard, MilestoneProgress, NextStepsPanel\\n**Files**: `components/ProjectDetailsPanel.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 9: Project View Main Component\\n**Description**: Main page component orchestrating the entire Project View\\n**Complexity**: Complex\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Two-panel layout: ProjectList (left) + ProjectDetailsPanel (right)\\n- Manages project selection state\\n- Handles routing and URL parameters for deep linking\\n- Mobile responsive with drawer/modal project list\\n- Loading states during initial data fetch\\n- Error boundaries for component failures\\n\\n**Dependencies**: ProjectList, ProjectDetailsPanel\\n**Files**: `pages/ProjectView.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## API Integration and Services\\n\\n### Task 10: Project API Service\\n**Description**: API service layer for project-related endpoints\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Implements project list fetching (`GET /api/projects/summary`)\\n- Implements project details fetching (`GET /api/projects/{id}/details`)\\n- Implements project continuation (`POST /api/projects/{id}/continue`)\\n- Error handling with appropriate user messages\\n- Request caching for performance\\n- TypeScript interfaces for project data\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n**Files**: `services/projectService.js`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 11: Project Data Hooks\\n**Description**: React hooks for project data management\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- `useProjects()` hook for project list\\n- `useProjectDetails(projectId)` hook for specific project\\n- `useContinueProject()` hook for project continuation\\n- Loading, error, and success states\\n- Automatic refetching on mutations\\n- Optimistic updates for better UX\\n\\n**Dependencies**: projectService\\n**Files**: `hooks/useProjects.js`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Integration and Routing\\n\\n### Task 12: Navigation Integration\\n**Description**: Add Project View to main application navigation\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Add \\"Projects\\" tab to main navigation\\n- Route configuration for `/projects` and `/projects/:id`\\n- Active tab highlighting\\n- Breadcrumb support for project details\\n- Back navigation handling\\n\\n**Dependencies**: ProjectView component\\n**Files**: `App.jsx`, `routes.js`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Testing Components\\n\\n### Task 13: Unit Tests for Core Components\\n**Description**: Jest unit tests for reusable components\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Tests for Badge, ProgressBar, SDLCIndicator components\\n- Props validation and rendering tests\\n- Accessibility tests (screen reader compatibility)\\n- Snapshot testing for visual regression\\n- 90%+ code coverage for components\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Core components (Tasks 1-3)\\n**Files**: `__tests__/components/`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 14: Integration Tests for Main Components\\n**Description**: Integration tests for main page components and API integration\\n**Complexity**: Complex\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Tests for ProjectView end-to-end functionality\\n- Mock API responses and error scenarios\\n- User interaction testing (project selection, continue button)\\n- Mobile responsive behavior testing\\n- Loading state and error boundary testing\\n\\n**Dependencies**: ProjectView, API services (Tasks 8-11)\\n**Files**: `__tests__/integration/`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Total Tasks**: 14\\n**Dependencies**: \\n- Tasks 1-3, 7, 10: No dependencies (can start immediately)\\n- Tasks 4-6: Depend on Badge and other core components\\n- Tasks 8-9: Depend on sub-components\\n- Tasks 11: Depends on API service\\n- Task 12: Depends on main ProjectView\\n- Tasks 13-14: Depend on respective implementation tasks\\n\\n**Recommended Implementation Order**:\\n1. Core components (Tasks 1-3, 10)\\n2. Mid-level components (Tasks 4-7, 11)\\n3. Main components (Tasks 8-9)\\n4. Integration (Task 12)\\n5. Testing (Tasks 13-14)\\n\\n**Complexity Distribution**:\\n- Simple: 3 tasks\\n- Medium: 8 tasks\\n- Complex: 3 tasks\\n\\n**Frontend Technology Stack**:\\n- React with hooks\\n- React Router for navigation\\n- Fetch API for HTTP requests\\n- CSS Modules or Tailwind for styling\\n- Jest + React Testing Library for testing\\n- Dark theme consistency with existing UI"'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015GUvRtrQnPoBTGmGVYKmaF', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1_20260116_030132.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1_20260116_030132.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.2%\n- Average iterations per task: 4.3\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'stri