{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:01:37", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-bf70e339-9bb2-44c9-82af-c6e202e9364d', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Core Infrastructure & Decomposition Engine",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/smart_task_decomposition_milestones.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GLQdrgq9F5S2XA7WX7SXes', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GLQdrgq9F5S2XA7WX7SXes', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent Backend Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Core Design Philosophy\\n- Modular, event-driven backend architecture\\n- High observability and resilience\\n- Minimal performance overhead\\n- Seamless error recovery\\n\\n### High-Level Architecture Pattern\\n- Event-Driven Microservices\\n- CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) for metrics and state management\\n- Pub/Sub for real-time progress streaming\\n\\n## 2. Technology Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+ (type hints, asyncio)\\n- **Async Framework**: `asyncio` + `uvloop` for high-performance concurrency\\n- **WebSocket**: `websockets` library\\n- **Event Bus**: `aio-pika` (AMQP-based message queue)\\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + `prometheus_client`\\n- **Persistence**: SQLAlchemy with PostgreSQL\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- Python chosen for its strong async capabilities and rich AI/ML ecosystem\\n- `asyncio` provides efficient concurrent execution without heavy threading\\n- Prometheus offers robust metrics collection with minimal overhead\\n- PostgreSQL ensures strong consistency for state persistence\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### 1. AgentRuntime (Enhanced)\\n- Responsible for agent lifecycle management\\n- Emits granular progress events\\n- Handles automatic error recovery\\n- Coordinates state checkpointing\\n\\n### 2. StateManager\\n- Manages agent state persistence\\n- Implements checkpoint/resume functionality\\n- Supports partial state reconstruction\\n- Handles context preservation during retries\\n\\n### 3. ProgressEventBus\\n- Centralized event streaming mechanism\\n- Publishes real-time agent progress\\n- Supports WebSocket broadcasting\\n- Low-latency event routing\\n\\n### 4. AgentAnalytics\\n- Collects performance metrics\\n- Tracks token usage, success rates\\n- Provides adaptive model selection logic\\n- Generates performance reports\\n\\n### 5. ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Classifies errors (retriable vs fatal)\\n- Manages retry strategies\\n- Implements exponential backoff\\n- Tracks error history for optimization\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\nAgent Spawn Request\\n    \\u2193\\n[AgentRuntime]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Start Execution\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Emit Progress Events \\u2192 [ProgressEventBus]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Checkpoint State \\u2192 [StateManager]\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Track Metrics \\u2192 [AgentAnalytics]\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 On Error \\u2192 [ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator]\\n        \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Retry Logic\\n        \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 State Resume\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Performance Tracking\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Token Usage\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Success Rates\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Model Performance\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Key Implementation Details\\n\\n### Progress Streaming\\n- Use WebSocket for real-time updates\\n- Event types:\\n  - `agent_spawn`\\n  - `tool_invocation_start`\\n  - `tool_invocation_complete`\\n  - `agent_state_change`\\n  - `error_occurred`\\n\\n### Error Recovery Strategy\\n- Checkpoint every significant state transition\\n- Store:\\n  - Conversation history\\n  - Tool execution results\\n  - Spawned agent context\\n- Retry mechanism:\\n  1. Exponential backoff\\n  2. Maximum retry limit\\n  3. Fallback to manual intervention\\n\\n### Analytics Collection\\n- Metrics per agent:\\n  - Execution time\\n  - Token consumption\\n  - Success/failure rate\\n  - Model tier performance\\n- Aggregation levels:\\n  - Per agent instance\\n  - Per agent type\\n  - Across system\\n\\n## 6. Deployment Considerations\\n\\n### Container Strategy\\n- Docker containers for each component\\n- Docker Compose for local development\\n- Kubernetes for production scaling\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n- Use `.env` files for configuration\\n- Support multiple environments:\\n  - Development\\n  - Staging\\n  - Production\\n\\n## 7. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Testing Approaches\\n- Unit Tests: `pytest`\\n- Integration Tests: `pytest-asyncio`\\n- Performance Tests: `locust`\\n- Coverage: `coverage.py`\\n\\n### Test Coverage Requirements\\n- 90%+ unit test coverage\\n- Integration tests for error recovery\\n- Chaos testing for resilience verification\\n\\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. Performance Overhead from Metrics\\n   - **Mitigation**: Sampling, async metrics collection\\n2. WebSocket Connection Instability\\n   - **Mitigation**: Reconnection logic, connection pooling\\n3. State Persistence Complexity\\n   - **Mitigation**: Robust serialization, comprehensive testing\\n\\n## 9. Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. Preferred message queue technology (current proposal: AMQP)\\n2. Specific performance budget for metrics collection\\n3. Desired granularity of progress events\\n\\n## 10. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Synchronous Execution\\n- **Pros**: Simpler implementation\\n- **Cons**: Poor concurrency, blocking operations\\n- **Verdict**: Rejected in favor of async design\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Separate Metrics Service\\n- **Pros**: Clearer separation of concerns\\n- **Cons**: Additional complexity, network overhead\\n- **Verdict**: Current design integrated for performance\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, performant backend for the ensemble agent system, focusing on real-time visibility, error resilience, and continuous improvement through comprehensive analytics."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DUx2BbSvKrfyPmDAqe6z1S', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/smart_task_decomposition_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DUx2BbSvKrfyPmDAqe6z1S', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nImplement a comprehensive Task Decomposition Engine for Ensemble AI that analyzes complex user requests, generates dependency graphs, estimates resources, and presents execution plans for user approval.\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Core Infrastructure & Decomposition Engine\\n**Objective**: Build the core decomposition engine with task analysis and dependency graph generation.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_engine.py` - Core engine with:\\n   - Pydantic data models (TaskAnalysis, SubTask, DecompositionPlan, ResourceEstimate, AllocationPlan, Schedule)\\n   - `TaskDecompositionEngine` class with all core methods\\n   - NetworkX-based DAG generation and validation\\n   - Resource estimation and allocation optimization\\n   - Execution schedule generation\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Can analyze task complexity and domain\\n- Generates valid DAGs (no cycles)\\n- Produces resource estimates with cost calculations\\n- Creates parallel execution waves\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Learning Module\\n**Objective**: Build the learning module for continuous improvement of estimates.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_learner.py` - Learning module with:\\n   - `DecompositionLearner` class\\n   - Execution recording and history storage\\n   - Estimate improvement based on historical data\\n   - Accuracy metrics tracking\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Records execution outcomes\\n- Improves estimates over time\\n- Provides accuracy metrics\\n- Suggests improvements based on patterns\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (uses DecompositionPlan models)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Executive Director Integration\\n**Objective**: Integrate decomposition engine into Executive Director workflow.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Updated `leadership/executive_director.md` with:\\n   - New decomposition workflow\\n   - Extended output format with `decomposition_plan` field\\n   - User approval flow for plans\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Executive Director uses decomposition before spawning agents\\n- Output includes decomposition plan\\n- Supports plan approval workflow\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 4: API Endpoints\\n**Objective**: Add backend API endpoints for decomposition functionality.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Updated `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py` with:\\n   - `POST /api/decompose` - Decompose user request\\n   - `POST /api/approve-plan` - Accept/reject/modify plans\\n   - `GET /api/decomposition-history` - Historical accuracy\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All endpoints functional\\n- Proper error handling\\n- Integration with decomposition engine\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 5: Frontend Visualization\\n**Objective**: Build React component for task decomposition visualization.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx` with:\\n   - Mermaid diagram rendering\\n   - Resource estimates display\\n   - Execution wave visualization\\n   - Agent assignment table\\n   - Approve/Reject/Modify buttons\\n   - Plan modification interface\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Renders dependency graph with Mermaid\\n- Displays resource estimates\\n- Action buttons work correctly\\n- Responsive UI\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 4 (needs API endpoints)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 6: Test Suite\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing for all decomposition functionality.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `tests/test_decomposition.py` with:\\n   - Unit tests for each method\\n   - Integration tests for full flow\\n   - Graph validity tests\\n   - Benchmark tests (simple, medium, complex)\\n   - Learning accuracy tests\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All unit tests pass\\n- Integration tests cover full workflow\\n- DAG validity verified\\n- Performance benchmarks documented\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2, 4\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 7: Documentation\\n**Objective**: Complete documentation for the decomposition engine.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md` with:\\n   - Architecture overview\\n   - Usage examples\\n   - API reference\\n   - Configuration options\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Clear architecture explanation\\n- Working code examples\\n- Complete API documentation\\n- Configuration fully documented\\n\\n**Dependencies**: All previous milestones\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Execution Order\\n1. Milestone 1 (Core Engine) - Foundation\\n2. Milestone 2 (Learning Module) - Builds on engine\\n3. Milestones 3, 4 (Integration + API) - Can run in parallel\\n4. Milestone 5 (Frontend) - Needs API\\n5. Milestone 6 (Tests) - Needs all code\\n6. Milestone 7 (Documentation) - Final\\n\\n## Estimated Timeline\\n- Milestones 1-2: Core implementation\\n- Milestones 3-5: Integration and UI\\n- Milestones 6-7: Quality and documentation\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n- **Medium Risk**: NetworkX/PuLP integration complexity\\n- **Low Risk**: Standard patterns for API/UI\\n- **Mitigation**: Use existing project patterns, fallback to simpler algorithms if needed\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Wc3A6U7JSGEwTCCtkvZZwx', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy for Core Infrastructure & Decomposition Engine (Milestone 1)\n\n## Test Objectives\nEnsure robust implementation of the Task Decomposition Engine with comprehensive test coverage for:\n- Data models\n- Core decomposition logic\n- DAG generation\n- Resource estimation\n- Execution scheduling\n\n## Unit Test Categories\n\n### 1. Pydantic Data Model Tests\n- Validate model creation\n- Test field constraints\n- Verify serialization/deserialization\n- Check default value handling\n\n### 2. Task Analysis Tests\n- Complexity calculation\n- Domain identification\n- Input validation\n- Edge case handling\n\n### 3. DAG Generation Tests\n- Graph creation validation\n- Cycle detection\n- Dependency resolution\n- Parallelization logic\n- Complex graph scenarios\n\n### 4. Resource Estimation Tests\n- Cost calculation accuracy\n- Resource type mapping\n- Over/under allocation detection\n- Optimization strategy verification\n\n### 5. Execution Schedule Tests\n- Wave generation\n- Parallel execution validation\n- Time estimation\n- Resource constraint handling\n\n## Integration Tests\n- Full workflow simulation\n- End-to-end decomposition process\n- Integration with NetworkX\n- Interaction between components\n\n## Performance Tests\n- Large task graph generation\n- Resource allocation for complex scenarios\n- Computational complexity analysis\n\n## Test Coverage Goals\n- Unit Test Coverage: 90%\n- Integration Coverage: 100%\n- Branch Coverage: 85%\n\n## Testing Tools\n- Framework: pytest\n- Mocking: unittest.mock\n- Graph Testing: NetworkX test utilities\n- Performance: pytest-benchmark\n\n## Key Testing Dimensions\n1. Correctness\n2. Performance\n3. Error Handling\n4. Edge Case Coverage\n\n## Test Task Breakdown\n1. Data Model Validation Tests\n2. Task Analysis Logic Tests\n3. DAG Generation Tests\n4. Resource Estimation Tests\n5. Scheduling Algorithm Tests\n6. Integration Workflow Tests\n7. Performance Benchmark Tests\n8. Error Scenario Tests\n\n## Risks to Mitigate\n- Complex graph generation\n- Resource allocation accuracy\n- Performance with large task sets\n\n## Out of Scope\n- External system integrations\n- Machine learning prediction accuracy'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Wc3A6U7JSGEwTCCtkvZZwx', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260116_030134.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260116_030134.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou 