vent bus\n- Verify activity tracker integration\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Agent spawn events contain whimsical names\n- Multiple agents have unique names\n- Names appear in progress events\n- Activity tracker shows whimsical names\n\n#### IT-002: State Persistence with Whimsical Names\n**Component**: AgentRuntime + StateManager\n**Priority**: HIGH\n**Assigned to**: TDD Coordinator\n**Description**: Test state persistence using whimsical names as identifiers\n**Test Cases**:\n- Create agent, checkpoint state with whimsical name\n- Resume agent from checkpoint using whimsical name\n- Test state lookup by whimsical agent_id\n- Verify state consistency across restarts\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- State persisted with whimsical agent_id as key\n- Successful resume from whimsical-named checkpoints\n- No state corruption with name changes\n- Consistent state retrieval\n\n#### IT-003: Event Broadcasting with Whimsical Names\n**Component**: ProgressEventBus + AgentRuntime\n**Priority**: HIGH\n**Assigned to**: TDD Coordinator\n**Description**: Test real-time event streaming with whimsical agent names\n**Test Cases**:\n- Subscribe to agent events by whimsical name\n- Test event filtering by agent_id\n- Verify WebSocket broadcasts include whimsical names\n- Test event ordering with multiple named agents\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Events contain whimsical agent names\n- Event filtering works with whimsical IDs\n- WebSocket clients receive correct names\n- Event ordering preserved per agent\n\n#### IT-004: Analytics Integration\n**Component**: AgentAnalytics + AgentRuntime\n**Priority**: MEDIUM\n**Assigned to**: TDD Coordinator\n**Description**: Test metrics collection with whimsical agent names\n**Test Cases**:\n- Collect performance metrics by whimsical name\n- Test token usage tracking per named agent\n- Verify success rate calculations\n- Test metric aggregation with whimsical IDs\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Metrics tagged with whimsical agent names\n- Accurate token usage per named agent\n- Success rate calculations work correctly\n- Aggregation includes agent type metadata\n\n#### IT-005: Error Recovery with Named Agents\n**Component**: ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator + AgentRuntime\n**Priority**: HIGH\n**Assigned to**: TDD Coordinator\n**Description**: Test error recovery flows with whimsical agent names\n**Test Cases**:\n- Trigger error in named agent, test recovery\n- Verify retry logic preserves whimsical name\n- Test error classification with named agents\n- Validate recovery state consistency\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Error recovery preserves whimsical agent names\n- Retry attempts maintain same agent_id\n- Error logs include whimsical names\n- Recovery state is consistent\n\n#### IT-006: Database Integration\n**Component**: StateManager + PostgreSQL\n**Priority**: MEDIUM\n**Assigned to**: TDD Coordinator\n**Description**: Test database operations with whimsical agent identifiers\n**Test Cases**:\n- Store agent data with whimsical ID as primary key\n- Query agents by whimsical name\n- Test database constraints with name format\n- Verify indexing performance\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Database stores whimsical names correctly\n- Queries by whimsical ID are fast (< 10ms)\n- No database constraint violations\n- Proper indexing on agent_id field\n\n### End-to-End Tests (4 tasks)\n\n#### E2E-001: Complete Agent Lifecycle in UI\n**Component**: Full system (UI + Backend)\n**Priority**: HIGH\n**Assigned to**: TDD Coordinator\n**Description**: Test complete user journey with whimsical agent names\n**Test Cases**:\n- Create project in UI, spawn agents\n- Verify whimsical names appear in UI\n- Test agent hierarchy display\n- Complete project with named agents\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- UI displays whimsical names instead of timestamps\n- Agent hierarchy shows readable names\n- Project completion works with named agents\n- User experience improved with memorable names\n\n#### E2E-002: Multi-Agent Collaboration\n**Component**: Full system\n**Priority**: HIGH\n**Assigned to**: TDD Coordinator\n**Description**: Test multiple agents working together with whimsical names\n**Test Cases**:\n- Spawn multiple agent types simultaneously\n- Test inter-agent communication with names\n- Verify unique naming across agent types\n- Test agent spawning of child agents\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All agents have unique whimsical names\n- Inter-agent communication uses whimsical IDs\n- Parent-child relationships preserved\n- No naming conflicts across types\n\n#### E2E-003: Error Scenarios with Named Agents\n**Component**: Full system\n**Priority**: MEDIUM\n**Assigned to**: TDD Coordinator\n**Description**: Test error handling in real scenarios with whimsical names\n**Test Cases**:\n- Trigger API failures with named agents\n- Test recovery flow in UI\n- Verify error messages include whimsical names\n- Test manual intervention scenarios\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Error messages show whimsical names\n- Recovery flows preserve agent names\n- UI handles error states gracefully\n- Manual intervention works with names\n\n#### E2E-004: Performance under Load\n**Component**: Full system\n**Priority**: LOW\n**Assigned to**: TDD Coordinator\n**Description**: Test system performance with whimsical naming under load\n**Test Cases**:\n- Create 50 concurrent agents\n- Monitor naming performance\n- Test UI responsiveness with many named agents\n- Verify no memory leaks\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Name generation scales to 50+ agents\n- UI remains responsive with many agents\n- No memory leaks detected\n- Overall performance within 10% of baseline\n\n## Test Coverage Goals\n\n### Unit Test Coverage: 90%+\n- AgentNameGenerator: 95%\n- AgentRuntime naming integration: 90%\n- Name data module: 85%\n- Error handling: 90%\n\n### Integration Test Coverage: 100%\n- All agent spawning flows\n- State persistence with names\n- Event broadcasting\n- Analytics collection\n- Error recovery\n\n### End-to-End Test Coverage: Critical paths only\n- Agent lifecycle in UI\n- Multi-agent collaboration\n- Error recovery scenarios\n- Basic performance validation\n\n## Test Infrastructure Requirements\n\n### Test Framework\n- **Backend**: `pytest` with `pytest-asyncio` for async testing\n- **Coverage**: `coverage.py` for coverage reporting\n- **Performance**: Basic timing assertions (< 1ms name generation)\n- **Concurrency**: `threading` module for concurrent test scenarios\n\n### Test Data\n- Use existing WHIMSICAL_NAMES list for validation\n- Mock external dependencies (database, WebSocket connections)\n- Test fixtures for common agent configurations\n- Deterministic random seeds for reproducible tests\n\n### CI/CD Integration\n- Run all unit tests on every commit\n- Run integration tests on pull requests\n- Run E2E tests on release branches\n- Coverage threshold: 90% for unit tests\n\n## Quality Gates\n\n### Unit Tests Must Pass\n- All 8 unit test tasks complete with 90%+ coverage\n- No test failures or flaky tests\n- Performance requirements met (< 1ms name generation)\n\n### Integration Tests Must Pass  \n- All 6 integration test tasks complete\n- No integration failures\n- State persistence working correctly\n- Event streaming functional\n\n### End-to-End Validation\n- UI displays whimsical names correctly\n- No regression in user experience\n- Multi-agent scenarios work\n- Error handling maintains names\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### Test Execution Order\n1. Unit tests first (fastest feedback)\n2. Integration tests second (moderate speed)\n3. End-to-end tests last (slowest, most comprehensive)\n\n### Test Isolation\n- Each test should be independent\n- Clean up generated names after tests\n- Reset singleton state between test runs\n- Use fresh database for integration tests\n\n### Performance Monitoring\n- Monitor name generation latency\n- Track memory usage during concurrent tests\n- Validate no performance regression in agent spawning\n- Benchmark against timestamp-based generation\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n### Functional Success\n- 18 test tasks implemented and passing\n- 90%+ unit test coverage achieved\n- 100% integration test coverage\n- Critical E2E scenarios validated\n\n### Non-Functional Success\n- Name generation < 1ms\n- No memory leaks under load\n- Thread-safe concurrent operation\n- UI performance maintained\n\n### User Experience Success\n- Whimsical names appear in UI\n- Names are memorable and distinct\n- Error messages use readable names\n- Overall improved user experience\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Risk: Test complexity with threading\n**Mitigation**: Use pytest-asyncio and careful test isolation\n\n### Risk: Flaky tests with randomization\n**Mitigation**: Use deterministic random seeds in tests\n\n### Risk: Database test setup complexity\n**Mitigation**: Use in-memory database for faster integration tests\n\n### Risk: UI testing requires browser automation\n**Mitigation**: Focus on backend API testing, minimal UI automation\n\n## Ready for Implementation\n\nThis test strategy provides comprehensive coverage of the whimsical name integration with:\n- 8 unit test tasks covering core logic and edge cases\n- 6 integration test tasks covering system interactions\n- 4 end-to-end test tasks covering user scenarios\n- Clear coverage goals and success criteria\n- Well-defined quality gates\n\n**Total: 18 test tasks ready for implementation by TDD Coordinator**"'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019d56h5yfMDkzUtzERxK1Vu', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260116_030202.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260116_030202.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.8\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
