{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:02:03", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8ca8bbf8-6736-4476-83f0-e21548bd6ca9', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Backend Infrastructure for Agent Cost Tracking",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md",\n  "project_name": "Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RgG9K5FcpdJU995f8Z5RKf', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RgG9K5FcpdJU995f8Z5RKf', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent Backend Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Core Design Philosophy\\n- Modular, event-driven backend architecture\\n- High observability and resilience\\n- Minimal performance overhead\\n- Seamless error recovery\\n\\n### High-Level Architecture Pattern\\n- Event-Driven Microservices\\n- CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) for metrics and state management\\n- Pub/Sub for real-time progress streaming\\n\\n## 2. Technology Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+ (type hints, asyncio)\\n- **Async Framework**: `asyncio` + `uvloop` for high-performance concurrency\\n- **WebSocket**: `websockets` library\\n- **Event Bus**: `aio-pika` (AMQP-based message queue)\\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + `prometheus_client`\\n- **Persistence**: SQLAlchemy with PostgreSQL\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- Python chosen for its strong async capabilities and rich AI/ML ecosystem\\n- `asyncio` provides efficient concurrent execution without heavy threading\\n- Prometheus offers robust metrics collection with minimal overhead\\n- PostgreSQL ensures strong consistency for state persistence\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### 1. AgentRuntime (Enhanced)\\n- Responsible for agent lifecycle management\\n- Emits granular progress events\\n- Handles automatic error recovery\\n- Coordinates state checkpointing\\n\\n### 2. StateManager\\n- Manages agent state persistence\\n- Implements checkpoint/resume functionality\\n- Supports partial state reconstruction\\n- Handles context preservation during retries\\n\\n### 3. ProgressEventBus\\n- Centralized event streaming mechanism\\n- Publishes real-time agent progress\\n- Supports WebSocket broadcasting\\n- Low-latency event routing\\n\\n### 4. AgentAnalytics\\n- Collects performance metrics\\n- Tracks token usage, success rates\\n- Provides adaptive model selection logic\\n- Generates performance reports\\n\\n### 5. ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Classifies errors (retriable vs fatal)\\n- Manages retry strategies\\n- Implements exponential backoff\\n- Tracks error history for optimization\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\nAgent Spawn Request\\n    \\u2193\\n[AgentRuntime]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Start Execution\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Emit Progress Events \\u2192 [ProgressEventBus]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Checkpoint State \\u2192 [StateManager]\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Track Metrics \\u2192 [AgentAnalytics]\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 On Error \\u2192 [ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator]\\n        \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Retry Logic\\n        \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 State Resume\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Performance Tracking\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Token Usage\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Success Rates\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Model Performance\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Key Implementation Details\\n\\n### Progress Streaming\\n- Use WebSocket for real-time updates\\n- Event types:\\n  - `agent_spawn`\\n  - `tool_invocation_start`\\n  - `tool_invocation_complete`\\n  - `agent_state_change`\\n  - `error_occurred`\\n\\n### Error Recovery Strategy\\n- Checkpoint every significant state transition\\n- Store:\\n  - Conversation history\\n  - Tool execution results\\n  - Spawned agent context\\n- Retry mechanism:\\n  1. Exponential backoff\\n  2. Maximum retry limit\\n  3. Fallback to manual intervention\\n\\n### Analytics Collection\\n- Metrics per agent:\\n  - Execution time\\n  - Token consumption\\n  - Success/failure rate\\n  - Model tier performance\\n- Aggregation levels:\\n  - Per agent instance\\n  - Per agent type\\n  - Across system\\n\\n## 6. Deployment Considerations\\n\\n### Container Strategy\\n- Docker containers for each component\\n- Docker Compose for local development\\n- Kubernetes for production scaling\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n- Use `.env` files for configuration\\n- Support multiple environments:\\n  - Development\\n  - Staging\\n  - Production\\n\\n## 7. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Testing Approaches\\n- Unit Tests: `pytest`\\n- Integration Tests: `pytest-asyncio`\\n- Performance Tests: `locust`\\n- Coverage: `coverage.py`\\n\\n### Test Coverage Requirements\\n- 90%+ unit test coverage\\n- Integration tests for error recovery\\n- Chaos testing for resilience verification\\n\\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. Performance Overhead from Metrics\\n   - **Mitigation**: Sampling, async metrics collection\\n2. WebSocket Connection Instability\\n   - **Mitigation**: Reconnection logic, connection pooling\\n3. State Persistence Complexity\\n   - **Mitigation**: Robust serialization, comprehensive testing\\n\\n## 9. Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. Preferred message queue technology (current proposal: AMQP)\\n2. Specific performance budget for metrics collection\\n3. Desired granularity of progress events\\n\\n## 10. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Synchronous Execution\\n- **Pros**: Simpler implementation\\n- **Cons**: Poor concurrency, blocking operations\\n- **Verdict**: Rejected in favor of async design\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Separate Metrics Service\\n- **Pros**: Clearer separation of concerns\\n- **Cons**: Additional complexity, network overhead\\n- **Verdict**: Current design integrated for performance\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, performant backend for the ensemble agent system, focusing on real-time visibility, error resilience, and continuous improvement through comprehensive analytics."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FNm6vi2b6yRXmgJLoWXjGZ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FNm6vi2b6yRXmgJLoWXjGZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\\n\\n## Vision\\nEnhance the ensemble UI to display cost estimates, execution duration, and model information for each agent task. This will provide better visibility into agent performance and resource usage.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Display execution cost estimates for each agent in the agent summary\\n2. Show start time, completion time, and duration of execution\\n3. Tag each agent with the model it used during execution\\n4. Ensure data flows from backend tracking to frontend display\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n1. **Backend Enhancements**:\\n   - Capture start time, end time, and duration for agent executions\\n   - Track the model used by each agent (from AgentRuntime)\\n   - Calculate cost estimates based on token usage and model pricing\\n   - Include this data in activity tracking and agent states\\n\\n2. **Frontend Enhancements**:\\n   - Display cost estimate in AgentSummaryPane component\\n   - Show execution duration (started \\u2192 completed)\\n   - Display model tag/badge for each agent\\n   - Format costs in a user-friendly way (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n   - Format durations in appropriate units (ms, seconds, minutes)\\n\\n3. **Data Flow**:\\n   - Extend Activity Tracker to capture cost and model data\\n   - Update API endpoints to return this information\\n   - Update AgentSummaryPane to consume and display the data\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Historical cost aggregation/reporting (future feature)\\n- Budget alerts or limits (future feature)\\n- Per-tool cost breakdown (future feature)\\n- Real-time cost streaming during execution (will show on completion)\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must work with existing activity_tracker.py system\\n- Should integrate with existing AgentRuntime metrics\\n- Frontend changes limited to AgentSummaryPane component\\n- Backend must be backward compatible with existing agent executions\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. \\u2705 Each completed agent shows:\\n   - Start time (ISO format or relative time)\\n   - Completion time (ISO format or relative time)\\n   - Duration (e.g., \\"2.3s\\", \\"1m 45s\\")\\n   - Cost estimate (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n   - Model tag (e.g., \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\")\\n\\n2. \\u2705 Data is captured reliably from backend\\n3. \\u2705 UI displays information in a readable, compact format\\n4. \\u2705 No performance degradation to existing functionality\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n1. AgentRuntime already tracks token usage and model selection\\n2. Model pricing information is available (from model_selector.py or similar)\\n3. Activity tracker can be extended without breaking existing consumers\\n4. Frontend has access to activity data via WebSocket or polling\\n\\n## User Stories\\n1. **As a developer**, I want to see how much each agent execution costs so I can optimize expensive operations\\n2. **As a developer**, I want to see execution duration so I can identify slow agents\\n3. **As a developer**, I want to see which model was used so I can correlate performance with model choice\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Backend Changes\\n1. Extend `record_agent_completed()` in activity_tracker.py to accept:\\n   - `started_at`: ISO timestamp\\n   - `completed_at`: ISO timestamp  \\n   - `duration_ms`: milliseconds\\n   - `model_used`: model identifier\\n   - `cost_estimate`: float (USD)\\n\\n2. Update AgentRuntime to:\\n   - Track start time on initialization\\n   - Calculate cost based on token usage and model pricing\\n   - Pass this data to activity tracker on completion\\n\\n3. Update API response in main.py to include these fields in agent state\\n\\n### Frontend Changes\\n1. Update AgentSummaryPane.jsx to:\\n   - Display execution timeline (started \\u2192 completed)\\n   - Show duration badge\\n   - Show cost estimate badge\\n   - Show model tag\\n   - Handle formatting for readability\\n\\n### Data Structure\\n```javascript\\n// Expected agent info structure\\n{\\n  agent_id: \\"exec_dir_1\\",\\n  type: \\"executive_director\\",\\n  status: \\"completed\\",\\n  started_at: \\"2024-01-13T10:30:00Z\\",\\n  completed_at: \\"2024-01-13T10:30:42Z\\",\\n  duration_ms: 42000,\\n  model_used: \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\",\\n  cost_estimate: 0.0042,\\n  // ... existing fields\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n- Cost calculation should use actual token counts from Claude API responses\\n- If token counts unavailable, estimate based on character counts with clear \\"~\\" prefix\\n- Duration should handle both running (show elapsed) and completed states\\n- Model tags should be shortened for display (e.g., \\"sonnet-3.5\\" instead of full name)\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UXgjLn9ACe2jXUJPwsy3Xb', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement', 'description': 'Backend infrastructure for tracking and reporting agent execution costs, duration, and model information'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UXgjLn9ACe2jXUJPwsy3Xb', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "66d65b48", "message": "Created project: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement", "summary": {"project_id": "66d65b48", "project_name": "Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement", "description": "Backend infrastructure for tracking and reporting agent execution costs, duration, and model information", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T03:01:35.609385", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T03:01:35.609385", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T03:01:35.609385", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VFUxUUEtnfxT1FQe19PsHU', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\n\n## Database and ORM Modifications\n1. **Update Agent Tracking Model**\n   - Description: Extend existing agent tracking schema to include cost and performance metrics\n   - Complexity: Medium\n   - Acceptance Criteria:\n     * Model supports storing start_time, end_time, duration\n     * Can capture model_used and cost_estimate\n     * Maintains backward compatibility\n   - Dependencies: None\n\n2. **Model Pricing Configuration**\n   - Description: Create configuration mechanism for model pricing details\n   - Complexity: Simple\n   - Acceptance Criteria:\n     * Support configuring cost per 1000 tokens for different models\n     * Allow dynamic updates to pricing information\n     * Provide default fallback pricing\n   - Dependencies: [1. Update Agent Tracking Model]\n\n## Agent Runtime Cost Tracking\n3. **Token Usage Tracking**\n   - Description: Enhance AgentRuntime to capture detailed token consumption\n   - Complexity: Complex\n   - Acceptance Criteria:\n     * Track input and output token counts\n     * Differentiate token usage by model\n     * Provide mechanism to collect token data from API responses\n   - Dependencies: [1. Update Agent Tracking Model]\n\n4. **Cost Estimation Service**\n   - Description: Develop service to calculate execution cost based on token usage\n   - Complexity: Medium\n   - Acceptance Criteria:\n     * Calculate cost using model-specific pricing\n     * Handle edge cases (missing token data)\n     * Provide estimated cost with configurable precision\n   - Dependencies: [2. Model Pricing Configuration, 3. Token Usage Tracking]\n\n## API and Tracking Enhancements\n5. **Update Activity Tracker Endpoint**\n   - Description: Modify activity tracking to include cost and performance metrics\n   - Complexity: Medium\n   - Acceptance Criteria:\n     * Capture start_time, end_time, duration\n     * Include model_used and cost_estimate\n     * Ensure minimal performance overhead\n   - Dependencies: [1. Update Agent Tracking Model, 4. Cost Estimation Service]\n\n6. **WebSocket Progress Streaming Update**\n   - Description: Enhance WebSocket events to include cost and performance data\n   - Complexity: Simple\n   - Acceptance Criteria:\n     * Add new event types for cost updates\n     * Include performance metrics in agent state events\n     * Maintain existing WebSocket communication patterns\n   - Dependencies: [5. Update Activity Tracker Endpoint]\n\n## Error Handling and Validation\n7. **Cost Tracking Error Resilience**\n   - Description: Implement robust error handling for cost tracking mechanisms\n   - Complexity: Complex\n   - Acceptance Criteria:\n     * Gracefully handle missing token data\n     * Provide fallback cost estimation\n     * Log and track cost tracking errors\n   - Dependencies: [4. Cost Estimation Service]\n\n## Performance and Optimization\n8. **Metrics Collection Optimization**\n   - Description: Ensure minimal performance overhead for cost tracking\n   - Complexity: Complex\n   - Acceptance Criteria:\n     * Async token and cost tracking\n     * Configurable sampling for high-volume scenarios\n     * Performance benchmarks showing &lt;5% overhead\n   - Dependencies: [3. Token Usage Tracking, 7. Cost Tracking Error Resilience]\n\n## Compliance and Security\n9. **Data Privacy Protection**\n   - Description: Ensure sensitive cost and usage data is securely managed\n   - Complexity: Medium\n   - Acceptance Criteria:\n     * Implement data anonymization for cost metrics\n     * Secure storage of pricing configuration\n     * Role-based access to cost tracking data\n   - Dependencies: All previous tasks\n\n## Task Priority and Dependencies\n### Critical Path:\n1. Update Agent Tracking Model\n2. Token Usage Tracking\n3. Cost Estimation Service\n4. Update Activity Tracker Endpoint\n\n### Secondary Tasks:\n- Model Pricing Configuration\n- WebSocket Progress Streaming Update\n- Cost Tracking Error Resilience\n- Metrics Collection Optimization\n- Data Privacy Protection\n\n## Testing Strategy\n- Unit tests for each component\n- Integration tests for end-to-end cost tracking\n- Performance benchmarks\n- Error scenario validation'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VFUxUUEtnfxT1FQe19PsHU', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_030201.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_030201.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 93.1%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.7\n- Common errors to avoid: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
