{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:02:05", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-654ad143-1702-4619-ac0c-6e3391c6f5c6', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Root Cause Analysis & Backend Fix - Identify and fix the backend 404 issue for /api/activity/files endpoint",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_files_404_fix_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CthfA7e4cvN49vMbeL7ix2', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CthfA7e4cvN49vMbeL7ix2', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent Backend Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Core Design Philosophy\\n- Modular, event-driven backend architecture\\n- High observability and resilience\\n- Minimal performance overhead\\n- Seamless error recovery\\n\\n### High-Level Architecture Pattern\\n- Event-Driven Microservices\\n- CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) for metrics and state management\\n- Pub/Sub for real-time progress streaming\\n\\n## 2. Technology Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+ (type hints, asyncio)\\n- **Async Framework**: `asyncio` + `uvloop` for high-performance concurrency\\n- **WebSocket**: `websockets` library\\n- **Event Bus**: `aio-pika` (AMQP-based message queue)\\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + `prometheus_client`\\n- **Persistence**: SQLAlchemy with PostgreSQL\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- Python chosen for its strong async capabilities and rich AI/ML ecosystem\\n- `asyncio` provides efficient concurrent execution without heavy threading\\n- Prometheus offers robust metrics collection with minimal overhead\\n- PostgreSQL ensures strong consistency for state persistence\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### 1. AgentRuntime (Enhanced)\\n- Responsible for agent lifecycle management\\n- Emits granular progress events\\n- Handles automatic error recovery\\n- Coordinates state checkpointing\\n\\n### 2. StateManager\\n- Manages agent state persistence\\n- Implements checkpoint/resume functionality\\n- Supports partial state reconstruction\\n- Handles context preservation during retries\\n\\n### 3. ProgressEventBus\\n- Centralized event streaming mechanism\\n- Publishes real-time agent progress\\n- Supports WebSocket broadcasting\\n- Low-latency event routing\\n\\n### 4. AgentAnalytics\\n- Collects performance metrics\\n- Tracks token usage, success rates\\n- Provides adaptive model selection logic\\n- Generates performance reports\\n\\n### 5. ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Classifies errors (retriable vs fatal)\\n- Manages retry strategies\\n- Implements exponential backoff\\n- Tracks error history for optimization\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\nAgent Spawn Request\\n    \\u2193\\n[AgentRuntime]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Start Execution\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Emit Progress Events \\u2192 [ProgressEventBus]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Checkpoint State \\u2192 [StateManager]\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Track Metrics \\u2192 [AgentAnalytics]\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 On Error \\u2192 [ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator]\\n        \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Retry Logic\\n        \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 State Resume\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Performance Tracking\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Token Usage\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Success Rates\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Model Performance\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Key Implementation Details\\n\\n### Progress Streaming\\n- Use WebSocket for real-time updates\\n- Event types:\\n  - `agent_spawn`\\n  - `tool_invocation_start`\\n  - `tool_invocation_complete`\\n  - `agent_state_change`\\n  - `error_occurred`\\n\\n### Error Recovery Strategy\\n- Checkpoint every significant state transition\\n- Store:\\n  - Conversation history\\n  - Tool execution results\\n  - Spawned agent context\\n- Retry mechanism:\\n  1. Exponential backoff\\n  2. Maximum retry limit\\n  3. Fallback to manual intervention\\n\\n### Analytics Collection\\n- Metrics per agent:\\n  - Execution time\\n  - Token consumption\\n  - Success/failure rate\\n  - Model tier performance\\n- Aggregation levels:\\n  - Per agent instance\\n  - Per agent type\\n  - Across system\\n\\n## 6. Deployment Considerations\\n\\n### Container Strategy\\n- Docker containers for each component\\n- Docker Compose for local development\\n- Kubernetes for production scaling\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n- Use `.env` files for configuration\\n- Support multiple environments:\\n  - Development\\n  - Staging\\n  - Production\\n\\n## 7. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Testing Approaches\\n- Unit Tests: `pytest`\\n- Integration Tests: `pytest-asyncio`\\n- Performance Tests: `locust`\\n- Coverage: `coverage.py`\\n\\n### Test Coverage Requirements\\n- 90%+ unit test coverage\\n- Integration tests for error recovery\\n- Chaos testing for resilience verification\\n\\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. Performance Overhead from Metrics\\n   - **Mitigation**: Sampling, async metrics collection\\n2. WebSocket Connection Instability\\n   - **Mitigation**: Reconnection logic, connection pooling\\n3. State Persistence Complexity\\n   - **Mitigation**: Robust serialization, comprehensive testing\\n\\n## 9. Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. Preferred message queue technology (current proposal: AMQP)\\n2. Specific performance budget for metrics collection\\n3. Desired granularity of progress events\\n\\n## 10. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Synchronous Execution\\n- **Pros**: Simpler implementation\\n- **Cons**: Poor concurrency, blocking operations\\n- **Verdict**: Rejected in favor of async design\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Separate Metrics Service\\n- **Pros**: Clearer separation of concerns\\n- **Cons**: Additional complexity, network overhead\\n- **Verdict**: Current design integrated for performance\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, performant backend for the ensemble agent system, focusing on real-time visibility, error resilience, and continuous improvement through comprehensive analytics."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016TSBnaAf5ZWWrBG1XXuLzF', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_files_404_fix_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016TSBnaAf5ZWWrBG1XXuLzF', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Files Endpoint 404 Error - Bug Fix Requirements\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nUsers are seeing 404 \\"Not Found\\" errors in the UI when the frontend attempts to fetch generated files from the backend API. The error message appears as:\\n\\n```\\n{\\"detail\\":\\"Not Found\\"}\\n```\\n\\nPreceded by a BOM character (`\\\\ufeff`), indicating potential encoding or response format issues.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n- **User Report**: \\"Seeing a bunch of these errors in the ui when pinging files UI\\"\\n- **Affected Endpoint**: `/api/activity/files`\\n- **Frontend Location**: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/`\\n- **Backend Location**: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/`\\n- **Output Directory**: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/`\\n\\n## Technical Investigation Required\\n\\n### 1. Backend Status\\n- Verify backend server is running on expected port (8001)\\n- Check if endpoint registration is correct\\n- Validate endpoint handler function exists and is accessible\\n\\n### 2. Frontend API Calls\\n- Review `getGeneratedFiles()` function in `frontend/src/services/api.js`\\n- Verify correct URL construction and parameters\\n- Check polling interval and frequency (currently set to 1000ms in App.jsx)\\n\\n### 3. Potential Root Causes\\n- Backend server not running or crashed\\n- Endpoint URL mismatch between frontend and backend\\n- CORS configuration issues\\n- Activity tracker database connectivity problems\\n- Missing dependencies or import errors in backend\\n\\n## Files to Examine\\n\\n### Backend Files\\n1. `backend/main.py` - Main FastAPI application\\n   - Line 717: `@app.get(\\"/api/activity/files\\")` endpoint definition\\n   - Activity tracker integration\\n   - Error handling\\n\\n2. Backend runtime dependencies:\\n   - `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - Activity tracking system\\n   - `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` - AgentRuntime class\\n\\n### Frontend Files\\n1. `frontend/src/services/api.js` - API service layer\\n   - `getGeneratedFiles()` function\\n   - API_BASE_URL configuration\\n\\n2. `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Main application component\\n   - Polling logic for file updates\\n   - Error handling display\\n\\n3. `frontend/src/components/GeneratedFiles.jsx` - Files display component\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n1. Frontend polls `/api/activity/files` endpoint at configured interval\\n2. Backend returns JSON response with generated files:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\"files\\": [...],\\n     \\"count\\": 0\\n   }\\n   ```\\n3. UI displays files in the \\"Generated Files\\" section without errors\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **No 404 errors** when frontend polls files endpoint\\n2. **Correct response format** - JSON without BOM characters\\n3. **Files displayed** in UI when agents generate outputs\\n4. **Error handling** - Graceful degradation if backend temporarily unavailable\\n5. **Logging** - Clear error messages in both frontend console and backend logs\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n- **No breaking changes** to existing API contract\\n- **Maintain backwards compatibility** with current frontend implementation\\n- **Minimal code changes** - focus on fixing the specific 404 issue\\n- **Preserve existing functionality** - don\'t break other endpoints\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Adding new features to file display\\n- Redesigning the UI layout\\n- Changing polling architecture to WebSockets\\n- Performance optimization beyond fixing the bug\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- Backend is intended to run on port 8001\\n- Frontend is configured to connect to localhost:8001\\n- Activity tracker database exists and is accessible at `~/.ensemble/metrics.db`\\n- All required Python dependencies are installed\\n\\n## Acceptance Tests\\n\\n1. **Backend health check**: `curl http://localhost:8001/api/status` returns 200 OK\\n2. **Files endpoint test**: `curl http://localhost:8001/api/activity/files` returns JSON (not 404)\\n3. **Frontend test**: Open UI in browser, verify no 404 errors in console for `/api/activity/files`\\n4. **Integration test**: Generate a file via agent execution, verify it appears in UI without errors\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. **Root cause analysis** - Document why 404 was occurring\\n2. **Code fixes** - Implement solution in backend/frontend as needed\\n3. **Verification** - Test all affected endpoints work correctly\\n4. **Documentation** - Update any relevant docs about endpoint usage\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NDS4hzJJG8JUPeBnjJJ14a', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy - Root Cause Analysis & Backend Fix\n\n## Overview\nThis test strategy covers the identification and fix of the backend 404 issue for the `/api/activity/files` endpoint. The testing approach focuses on API endpoint functionality, integration between frontend and backend, and system resilience.\n\n## Test Coverage Goals\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 85% for backend API handlers and frontend API service functions\n- **Integration Test Coverage**: 100% of API endpoints, focusing on `/api/activity/files` \n- **E2E Test Coverage**: Critical user journey for file display functionality\n- **Error Scenario Coverage**: Network failures, backend unavailable, malformed responses\n\n## Test Categories\n\n### 1. Unit Tests\n\n#### Backend Unit Tests\n**Task 1.1: API Endpoint Handler Tests**\n- **Component**: `/api/activity/files` endpoint in `backend/main.py` (line 717)\n- **Framework**: pytest + pytest-asyncio\n- **Coverage**: \n  - Successful file retrieval\n  - Empty file list scenario\n  - Database connection errors\n  - Activity tracker integration\n- **Mocks**: Activity tracker database, file system operations\n- **Assertions**: Response format, status codes, error handling\n\n**Task 1.2: Activity Tracker Integration Tests**\n- **Component**: `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\n- **Framework**: pytest\n- **Coverage**:\n  - File tracking functionality\n  - Database operations\n  - Error scenarios (DB unavailable, corrupted data)\n- **Mocks**: SQLite database, file system\n- **Assertions**: Data persistence, retrieval accuracy\n\n#### Frontend Unit Tests\n**Task 1.3: API Service Function Tests**\n- **Component**: `getGeneratedFiles()` in `frontend/src/services/api.js`\n- **Framework**: Jest\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Successful API calls\n  - Network error handling\n  - Response parsing\n  - URL construction\n- **Mocks**: fetch API, network responses\n- **Assertions**: Correct API calls, error propagation\n\n**Task 1.4: Component Unit Tests**\n- **Component**: `frontend/src/components/GeneratedFiles.jsx`\n- **Framework**: Jest + React Testing Library\n- **Coverage**:\n  - File list rendering\n  - Loading states\n  - Error state display\n  - Empty state handling\n- **Mocks**: API service responses\n- **Assertions**: DOM content, state transitions\n\n### 2. Integration Tests\n\n**Task 2.1: Backend API Integration Tests**\n- **Scope**: Full backend server with real database\n- **Framework**: pytest + requests\n- **Coverage**:\n  - `/api/activity/files` endpoint behavior\n  - `/api/status` health check\n  - CORS configuration\n  - Response format validation\n- **Setup**: Test database, file fixtures\n- **Assertions**: HTTP status codes, JSON structure, headers\n\n**Task 2.2: Frontend-Backend Integration Tests**\n- **Scope**: Frontend API calls to running backend\n- **Framework**: Jest + MSW (Mock Service Worker) for controlled backend simulation\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Successful file fetching\n  - 404 error handling\n  - BOM character handling\n  - Polling behavior\n- **Setup**: Mock backend responses, timing controls\n- **Assertions**: UI state changes, error display\n\n**Task 2.3: Database Integration Tests**\n- **Scope**: Activity tracker with real SQLite database\n- **Framework**: pytest\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Database initialization\n  - File tracking persistence\n  - Concurrent access handling\n  - Database corruption recovery\n- **Setup**: Temporary test databases\n- **Assertions**: Data consistency, transaction safety\n\n### 3. End-to-End Tests\n\n**Task 3.1: Complete File Display Journey**\n- **Scope**: Full system - backend + frontend + browser\n- **Framework**: Playwright\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Start backend server\n  - Load frontend UI\n  - Verify no 404 errors in network tab\n  - Generate test file via agent\n  - Confirm file appears in UI\n- **Environment**: Full development stack\n- **Assertions**: No console errors, file visibility, correct content\n\n**Task 3.2: Error Recovery Scenarios**\n- **Scope**: System resilience testing\n- **Framework**: Playwright + backend process control\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Backend restart during polling\n  - Database lock scenarios\n  - Network interruption handling\n  - Graceful degradation behavior\n- **Environment**: Controlled failure injection\n- **Assertions**: Error messages, recovery behavior, system stability\n\n### 4. Performance Tests\n\n**Task 4.1: API Performance Validation**\n- **Scope**: `/api/activity/files` endpoint performance\n- **Framework**: pytest-benchmark\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Response time under normal load\n  - Memory usage during file listing\n  - Database query performance\n- **Metrics**: <200ms response time, <50MB memory usage\n- **Assertions**: Performance benchmarks met\n\n### 5. Security Tests\n\n**Task 5.1: API Security Validation**\n- **Scope**: Endpoint security\n- **Framework**: pytest + security test utilities\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Path traversal protection\n  - Input validation\n  - CORS policy validation\n  - Error information leakage\n- **Assertions**: No sensitive data exposure, proper access controls\n\n## Test Data and Fixtures\n\n### Backend Test Fixtures\n- Sample SQLite database with test activity data\n- Mock file system with generated files\n- Test configuration files\n\n### Frontend Test Fixtures\n- Mock API responses (success, error, empty)\n- Sample file data structures\n- Component props for various states\n\n### Integration Test Environment\n- Docker compose setup for isolated testing\n- Test database initialization scripts\n- Frontend build for testing\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n1. **All unit tests pass** with 85%+ code coverage\n2. **Integration tests validate** API endpoint functionality\n3. **E2E tests confirm** no 404 errors in browser\n4. **Performance tests meet** response time requirements\n5. **Security tests pass** basic vulnerability checks\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n\n### High Risk Areas\n- Database connection handling in activity tracker\n- Async operations in backend API handlers\n- Error handling in frontend API service\n- CORS configuration for cross-origin requests\n\n### Mitigation Strategies\n- Comprehensive error scenario testing\n- Database connection pooling tests\n- Network failure simulation\n- Browser compatibility verification\n\n## Automation Strategy\n\n### Continuous Integration\n- Unit tests run on every commit\n- Integration tests run on pull requests\n- E2E tests run on develop branch merges\n- Performance tests run nightly\n\n### Test Environment Management\n- Isolated test databases for each test run\n- Frontend test server automation\n- Backend test server lifecycle management\n\n## Tools and Dependencies\n\n### Backend Testing\n- pytest (test framework)\n- pytest-asyncio (async test support)\n- pytest-benchmark (performance testing)\n- requests (HTTP client for integration tests)\n- sqlite3 (test database)\n\n### Frontend Testing\n- Jest (test framework)\n- React Testing Library (component testing)\n- MSW (API mocking)\n- @testing-library/jest-dom (DOM assertions)\n\n### E2E Testing\n- Playwright (browser automation)\n- Docker (environment setup)\n- pytest-xvfb (headless browser support)\n\n### Coverage and Reporting\n- coverage.py (Python coverage)\n- jest coverage (JavaScript coverage)\n- junit-xml (CI/CD integration)\n\n## Test Execution Order\n\n1. **Unit Tests** - Fast feedback on code changes\n2. **Integration Tests** - Validate component interactions\n3. **Performance Tests** - Ensure no regression in speed\n4. **Security Tests** - Validate security requirements\n5. **E2E Tests** - Confirm full user experience\n\n## Estimated Effort\n\n- **Unit Tests**: 3-4 hours implementation, 1 hour maintenance\n- **Integration Tests**: 2-3 hours implementation, 30 minutes maintenance  \n- **E2E Tests**: 2-3 hours implementation, 1 hour maintenance\n- **Total**: 7-10 hours for complete test suite implementation\n\n## Test Maintenance Strategy\n\n- Update tests when API contracts change\n- Refresh test data fixtures monthly\n- Performance baseline updates quarterly\n- Security test updates with dependency changes'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NDS4hzJJG8JUPeBnjJJ14a', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260116_030205.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260116_030205.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.8\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
