{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:02:24", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8ecb36cb-0166-45e5-9036-ab3474b90de1', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Implement Dashboard and Cost Visualization",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01E3ttzSdVsXMs8uwuQmPbzS', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01E3ttzSdVsXMs8uwuQmPbzS', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent Backend Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Core Design Philosophy\\n- Modular, event-driven backend architecture\\n- High observability and resilience\\n- Minimal performance overhead\\n- Seamless error recovery\\n\\n### High-Level Architecture Pattern\\n- Event-Driven Microservices\\n- CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) for metrics and state management\\n- Pub/Sub for real-time progress streaming\\n\\n## 2. Technology Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+ (type hints, asyncio)\\n- **Async Framework**: `asyncio` + `uvloop` for high-performance concurrency\\n- **WebSocket**: `websockets` library\\n- **Event Bus**: `aio-pika` (AMQP-based message queue)\\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + `prometheus_client`\\n- **Persistence**: SQLAlchemy with PostgreSQL\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- Python chosen for its strong async capabilities and rich AI/ML ecosystem\\n- `asyncio` provides efficient concurrent execution without heavy threading\\n- Prometheus offers robust metrics collection with minimal overhead\\n- PostgreSQL ensures strong consistency for state persistence\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### 1. AgentRuntime (Enhanced)\\n- Responsible for agent lifecycle management\\n- Emits granular progress events\\n- Handles automatic error recovery\\n- Coordinates state checkpointing\\n\\n### 2. StateManager\\n- Manages agent state persistence\\n- Implements checkpoint/resume functionality\\n- Supports partial state reconstruction\\n- Handles context preservation during retries\\n\\n### 3. ProgressEventBus\\n- Centralized event streaming mechanism\\n- Publishes real-time agent progress\\n- Supports WebSocket broadcasting\\n- Low-latency event routing\\n\\n### 4. AgentAnalytics\\n- Collects performance metrics\\n- Tracks token usage, success rates\\n- Provides adaptive model selection logic\\n- Generates performance reports\\n\\n### 5. ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Classifies errors (retriable vs fatal)\\n- Manages retry strategies\\n- Implements exponential backoff\\n- Tracks error history for optimization\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\nAgent Spawn Request\\n    \\u2193\\n[AgentRuntime]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Start Execution\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Emit Progress Events \\u2192 [ProgressEventBus]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Checkpoint State \\u2192 [StateManager]\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Track Metrics \\u2192 [AgentAnalytics]\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 On Error \\u2192 [ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator]\\n        \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Retry Logic\\n        \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 State Resume\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Performance Tracking\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Token Usage\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Success Rates\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Model Performance\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Key Implementation Details\\n\\n### Progress Streaming\\n- Use WebSocket for real-time updates\\n- Event types:\\n  - `agent_spawn`\\n  - `tool_invocation_start`\\n  - `tool_invocation_complete`\\n  - `agent_state_change`\\n  - `error_occurred`\\n\\n### Error Recovery Strategy\\n- Checkpoint every significant state transition\\n- Store:\\n  - Conversation history\\n  - Tool execution results\\n  - Spawned agent context\\n- Retry mechanism:\\n  1. Exponential backoff\\n  2. Maximum retry limit\\n  3. Fallback to manual intervention\\n\\n### Analytics Collection\\n- Metrics per agent:\\n  - Execution time\\n  - Token consumption\\n  - Success/failure rate\\n  - Model tier performance\\n- Aggregation levels:\\n  - Per agent instance\\n  - Per agent type\\n  - Across system\\n\\n## 6. Deployment Considerations\\n\\n### Container Strategy\\n- Docker containers for each component\\n- Docker Compose for local development\\n- Kubernetes for production scaling\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n- Use `.env` files for configuration\\n- Support multiple environments:\\n  - Development\\n  - Staging\\n  - Production\\n\\n## 7. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Testing Approaches\\n- Unit Tests: `pytest`\\n- Integration Tests: `pytest-asyncio`\\n- Performance Tests: `locust`\\n- Coverage: `coverage.py`\\n\\n### Test Coverage Requirements\\n- 90%+ unit test coverage\\n- Integration tests for error recovery\\n- Chaos testing for resilience verification\\n\\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. Performance Overhead from Metrics\\n   - **Mitigation**: Sampling, async metrics collection\\n2. WebSocket Connection Instability\\n   - **Mitigation**: Reconnection logic, connection pooling\\n3. State Persistence Complexity\\n   - **Mitigation**: Robust serialization, comprehensive testing\\n\\n## 9. Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. Preferred message queue technology (current proposal: AMQP)\\n2. Specific performance budget for metrics collection\\n3. Desired granularity of progress events\\n\\n## 10. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Synchronous Execution\\n- **Pros**: Simpler implementation\\n- **Cons**: Poor concurrency, blocking operations\\n- **Verdict**: Rejected in favor of async design\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Separate Metrics Service\\n- **Pros**: Clearer separation of concerns\\n- **Cons**: Additional complexity, network overhead\\n- **Verdict**: Current design integrated for performance\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, performant backend for the ensemble agent system, focusing on real-time visibility, error resilience, and continuous improvement through comprehensive analytics."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PEQUndu3gsvg6R95TzYapi', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PEQUndu3gsvg6R95TzYapi', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Ensemble AI Provider Enhancement System\\n\\n## Vision\\nEnhance the ensemble system to support local CLI-based AI providers (Claude CLI, ChatGPT CLI) as preferred alternatives to direct API calls, implement comprehensive cost estimation and tracking, enable intelligent agent-task routing based on performance metrics, and resume previously paused work across 10 stalled projects.\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\nThis project addresses four key user needs:\\n1. **Local CLI Providers**: Use locally installed Claude/ChatGPT CLI tools as API substitutes, with preference for local tools when available and functional\\n2. **Cost Estimation**: Comprehensive pre-execution cost estimation and post-execution tracking\\n3. **Smart Agent Routing**: Data-driven routing to match agents with suitable work based on historical performance\\n4. **Work Resume**: Restart 10 previously stalled projects that were paused due to API credit issues\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### O1: Local CLI Provider Integration\\n- Detect locally installed Claude CLI (`/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` - confirmed present)\\n- Detect locally installed ChatGPT CLI (if available)\\n- Create adapter layer to use CLI tools as API substitutes\\n- Prefer CLI tools over API when available and functional\\n- Track success/failure statistics for CLI providers on metrics dashboard\\n\\n### O2: Cost Estimation Enhancement\\n- Pre-execution cost estimates based on task complexity and model selection\\n- Real-time cost tracking during execution\\n- Post-execution cost reporting\\n- Cost aggregation by project, agent type, and time period\\n- Cost visibility in metrics dashboard\\n\\n### O3: Intelligent Agent Routing\\n- Analyze historical agent performance data from metrics.db\\n- Route tasks to agents with best success rates for similar work\\n- Consider agent specialization (e.g., code_writer for code, tester for tests)\\n- Factor in cost efficiency when making routing decisions\\n- Provide routing recommendations with explanations\\n\\n### O4: Resume Paused Work\\n- Restart 10 stalled projects identified in task_recovery_analysis.md\\n- Sequential processing with independent error boundaries\\n- Generate recovery report documenting success/failure per project\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n#### Feature 1: CLI Provider Adapter System\\n- Auto-detect installed CLI tools on system startup\\n- Abstract provider interface supporting both API and CLI execution\\n- CLI provider for Claude (using `claude --print` or equivalent flags)\\n- CLI provider for ChatGPT (if available)\\n- Fallback chain: CLI \\u2192 API \\u2192 Error\\n- Provider health checks and availability testing\\n- Success/failure metrics per provider in dashboard\\n\\n#### Feature 2: Cost Estimation Module\\n- Pre-execution cost estimator based on:\\n  - Selected model (from model_selector.py)\\n  - Estimated input tokens (from prompt size)\\n  - Estimated output tokens (from task type heuristics)\\n- Cost tracking integration with existing cost_calculator.py\\n- Cost aggregation and reporting APIs\\n- Dashboard widgets for cost visualization\\n- Project-level cost attribution\\n\\n#### Feature 3: Smart Agent Router\\n- Performance analytics from metrics.db\\n- Agent-task matching algorithm considering:\\n  - Historical success rate per agent type\\n  - Task complexity vs agent capability\\n  - Cost efficiency per agent\\n  - Recent error patterns\\n- Routing recommendation API\\n- Override capability for manual agent selection\\n\\n#### Feature 4: Project Recovery Orchestration\\n- Parse task_recovery_analysis.md for 10 stalled projects\\n- Categorize by priority:\\n  - Priority 1: 3 in_progress tasks (likely stalled)\\n  - Priority 2: 5 todo tasks (not started)\\n  - Priority 3: 2 projects with no tasks\\n- Execute recovery sequentially\\n- Generate comprehensive recovery report\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Custom CLI tool development (use existing tools)\\n- Real-time API cost limits/caps (future enhancement)\\n- Parallel recovery execution (sequential for V1)\\n- CLI tool installation automation\\n\\n## Technical Design Overview\\n\\n### F1: CLI Provider Adapter\\n\\n#### Architecture\\n```\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502              AgentRuntime.execute()             \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u252c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n                      \\u2502\\n                      \\u25bc\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502           AIProviderManager (New)               \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510   \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502 detect_providers()                       \\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502 get_best_provider(model, task)           \\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502 execute(provider, prompt, model)         \\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518   \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u252c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n          \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u253c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n          \\u25bc           \\u25bc           \\u25bc\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510 \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510 \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502 ClaudeCLI   \\u2502 \\u2502 ChatGPTCLI  \\u2502 \\u2502 AnthropicAPI\\u2502\\n\\u2502 Provider    \\u2502 \\u2502 Provider    \\u2502 \\u2502 Provider    \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518 \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518 \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n```\\n\\n#### CLI Detection\\n```python\\n# Detect Claude CLI\\nwhich_claude = subprocess.run([\\"which\\", \\"claude\\"], capture_output=True)\\nclaude_available = which_claude.returncode == 0\\n\\n# Test Claude CLI functionality\\ntest_result = subprocess.run(\\n    [\\"claude\\", \\"--print\\", \\"-p\\", \\"Hello\\"],\\n    capture_output=True, timeout=10\\n)\\nclaude_functional = test_result.returncode == 0\\n```\\n\\n#### Provider Interface\\n```python\\nclass AIProvider(ABC):\\n    @abstractmethod\\n    def is_available(self) -> bool: ...\\n    \\n    @abstractmethod\\n    def execute(self, prompt: str, model: str, max_tokens: int) -> ProviderResponse: ...\\n    \\n    @abstractmethod\\n    def get_cost_estimate(self, input_tokens: int, output_tokens: int) -> float: ...\\n```\\n\\n#### Metrics Integration\\n- Track per-provider: success_count, failure_count, avg_response_time, total_tokens\\n- Add provider_type field to agent_executions table\\n- Dashboard: Provider usage pie chart, success rates comparison\\n\\n### F2: Cost Estimation Module\\n\\n#### Pre-Execution Estimation\\n```python\\nclass CostEstimator:\\n    def estimate_task_cost(\\n        self,\\n        model: str,\\n        prompt: str,\\n        task_complexity: str,\\n        expected_iterations: int = 1\\n    ) -> CostEstimate:\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Estimate cost before execution.\\n        \\n        Uses:\\n        - Actual prompt token count (tiktoken or approximation)\\n        - Task complexity to estimate output tokens\\n        - Model pricing from cost_calculator.py\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n```\\n\\n#### Task Complexity Heuristics\\n- **Strategic** tasks: Expect 4000-8000 output tokens\\n- **Creative** tasks: Expect 2000-4000 output tokens  \\n- **Routine** tasks: Expect 500-2000 output tokens\\n\\n#### Dashboard Integration\\n- Pre-execution estimate shown before spawning agents\\n- Running cost tracker during execution\\n- Final cost comparison (estimated vs actual)\\n- Cost trends over time (daily, weekly, monthly)\\n\\n### F3: Smart Agent Router\\n\\n#### Performance Analysis\\n```python\\nclass AgentRouter:\\n    def get_best_agent_for_task(\\n        self,\\n        task_type: str,\\n        task_complexity: str,\\n        available_agents: List[str]\\n    ) -> AgentRecommendation:\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Analyze metrics.db to find best agent for task.\\n        \\n        Considers:\\n        - Success rate for similar tasks\\n        - Average duration for task type\\n        - Cost efficiency\\n        - Recent error patterns\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n```\\n\\n#### Routing Algorithm\\n1. Query metrics.db for agent performance on similar tasks\\n2. Calculate composite score: `success_rate * 0.5 + cost_efficiency * 0.3 + speed * 0.2`\\n3. Apply specialization bonuses (e.g., code_writer +10% for code tasks)\\n4. Return ranked recommendations with explanations\\n\\n#### Agent Specialization Map\\n```python\\nAGENT_SPECIALIZATIONS = {\\n    \\"code_writer\\": [\\"implementation\\", \\"refactoring\\", \\"bug_fix\\"],\\n    \\"code_tester\\": [\\"unit_test\\", \\"integration_test\\", \\"test_fix\\"],\\n    \\"system_architect\\": [\\"architecture\\", \\"design\\", \\"planning\\"],\\n    \\"frontend_developer\\": [\\"ui\\", \\"ux\\", \\"react\\", \\"styling\\"],\\n    \\"backend_developer\\": [\\"api\\", \\"database\\", \\"server\\", \\"performance\\"]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### F4: Project Recovery\\n\\n#### Recovery Targets (from task_recovery_analysis.md)\\n| Priority | Project ID | Project Name | Issue |\\n|----------|------------|--------------|-------|\\n| 1 | bb528d28 | Local Weather Display Widget | Dev Manager stalled |\\n| 1 | 0114ab16 | Ensemble UI Enhancements | Architecture mismatch |\\n| 1 | 4af1c241 | Agent Hierarchy Organization | Dev Manager incomplete |\\n| 2 | 84dd6401 | Agent Tracking Metrics | Task not started |\\n| 2 | 5f5892f3 | Agent Cost Tracking - Frontend | Task not started |\\n| 2 | 66af6b69 | Agent Cost Tracking - Backend | Tasks not started |\\n| 2 | d863e0cc | Agent Completion Visibility | Tasks not started |\\n| 2 | ea916e81 | Ensemble UI Completion | Tasks not started |\\n| 3 | e30078c1 | Verifier Agent Swarm | No tasks created |\\n| 3 | 168565b8 | UI Activity Pane Graph | No tasks created |\\n\\n#### Recovery Strategy\\n- Priority 1: Spawn Development Manager to restart\\n- Priority 2: Spawn appropriate coordinator\\n- Priority 3: Spawn Executive Director for requirements\\n\\n## Users\\n- **Primary**: Ensemble system (automated provider selection, routing)\\n- **Secondary**: Developers (cost monitoring, performance analysis)\\n- **Tertiary**: End users (dashboard visibility)\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Must not break existing agent execution flow\\n- CLI providers must fall back gracefully to API\\n- Cost estimates should be within 50% of actual\\n- Recovery must be sequential (no parallel spawning)\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n### SC1: CLI Provider Integration\\n- [ ] Claude CLI detected and usable when available\\n- [ ] Graceful fallback to API when CLI unavailable\\n- [ ] Provider success/failure metrics visible in dashboard\\n- [ ] No increase in execution latency >10%\\n\\n### SC2: Cost Estimation\\n- [ ] Pre-execution cost estimates available for all tasks\\n- [ ] Estimates within 50% of actual costs\\n- [ ] Cost aggregation by project and time period\\n- [ ] Dashboard shows cost trends and breakdowns\\n\\n### SC3: Smart Agent Routing\\n- [ ] Agent recommendations based on historical performance\\n- [ ] Routing considers success rate, cost, and speed\\n- [ ] Override capability for manual selection\\n- [ ] 10% improvement in overall success rate\\n\\n### SC4: Project Recovery\\n- [ ] All 10 stalled projects restarted\\n- [ ] Recovery report generated with outcomes\\n- [ ] Independent error boundaries (one failure doesn\'t stop others)\\n- [ ] Progress visible in project tracking\\n\\n## Technical Assumptions\\n1. Claude CLI at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` supports `--print` flag for non-interactive mode\\n2. Existing metrics.db schema can be extended (add provider_type column)\\n3. Model pricing in cost_calculator.py is current\\n4. Project tracking system can update existing project IDs\\n\\n## Files to Create\\n- `src/runtime/agents/provider_manager.py` - Provider abstraction and detection\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cli_provider.py` - CLI provider implementations\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cost_estimator.py` - Pre-execution cost estimation\\n- `src/runtime/agents/agent_router.py` - Smart agent routing\\n- `src/runtime/agents/recovery_orchestrator.py` - Project recovery logic\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n- `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` - Integrate provider manager\\n- `src/runtime/agents/metrics.py` - Add provider tracking fields\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py` - Expose cost/routing APIs\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/App.jsx` - Dashboard widgets\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Claude CLI (`/opt/homebrew/bin/claude`) - confirmed available\\n- ChatGPT CLI (optional, detect if present)\\n- Existing ensemble infrastructure (runtime.py, metrics.py, etc.)\\n- SQLite database (~/.ensemble/metrics.db)\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n| Risk | Impact | Probability | Mitigation |\\n|------|--------|-------------|------------|\\n| CLI output format changes | High | Low | Parse flexibly, validate structure |\\n| CLI rate limiting | Medium | Medium | Implement backoff, fall back to API |\\n| Cost estimates significantly off | Medium | Medium | Calibrate with actual data |\\n| Recovery spawns fail | Medium | Medium | Independent boundaries, continue on error |\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Document Status**: Complete\\n**Created**: 2026-01-13\\n**Author**: Executive Director\\n**Version**: 1.0\\n**Project ID**: fcf1193e\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CxnUeZQ4RFgY3Sb45czHQB', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Frontend Tasks - Dashboard and Cost Visualization\n\n## Overview\nThis task breakdown covers the frontend implementation for the enhanced dashboard with cost visualization, provider management, agent routing metrics, and project recovery monitoring.\n\n## Architecture Context\n- **Framework**: React with hooks (based on existing ensemble_ui structure)\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS \n- **State Management**: Context API for simple state, Redux for complex analytics\n- **API Client**: fetch with error handling\n- **Charts**: Chart.js or Recharts for cost/performance visualizations\n- **Real-time**: WebSocket integration for live metrics\n\n## Task Groups\n\n### Group 1: Core Layout & Navigation (Foundation)\n\n#### Task 1.1: Enhanced Dashboard Layout Component\n**Description**: Create the main dashboard layout that accommodates new cost tracking, provider status, and analytics sections\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees organized dashboard with clear sections for providers, costs, agent performance, and project status\n- Layout is responsive and works on desktop/tablet\n- Navigation between dashboard sections is intuitive\n- Proper loading states and error boundaries\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/components/dashboard/DashboardLayout.jsx`\n\n#### Task 1.2: Navigation Enhancement\n**Description**: Update navigation to include links to new cost analytics and provider management sections\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User can navigate to Cost Analytics, Provider Status, Agent Performance tabs\n- Current section is highlighted\n- Breadcrumb navigation shows current location\n- Mobile-friendly navigation menu\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Files**: `src/components/navigation/Navigation.jsx`\n\n### Group 2: Provider Management UI\n\n#### Task 2.1: Provider Status Dashboard\n**Description**: Display real-time status of AI providers (CLI tools vs API)\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees current provider availability (Claude CLI, ChatGPT CLI, API fallbacks)\n- Provider health status with success/failure rates\n- Toggle to prefer CLI vs API when both available\n- Real-time updates via WebSocket\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/components/providers/ProviderStatus.jsx`\n\n#### Task 2.2: Provider Performance Metrics\n**Description**: Show detailed metrics per provider (response times, success rates, token usage)\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees comparative charts of provider performance\n- Filterable by date range and provider type\n- Success rate trends over time\n- Average response time comparison\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Files**: `src/components/providers/ProviderMetrics.jsx`\n\n### Group 3: Cost Visualization\n\n#### Task 3.1: Cost Overview Widget\n**Description**: High-level cost summary with current spending and trends\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees total costs for current day/week/month\n- Cost trend visualization (line chart)\n- Comparison to previous periods\n- Budget alerts if configured\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/components/costs/CostOverview.jsx`\n\n#### Task 3.2: Pre-Execution Cost Estimator\n**Description**: Show cost estimates before spawning agents\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees estimated cost before confirming agent spawn\n- Breakdown by model selection and task complexity\n- Option to adjust parameters to reduce cost\n- Clear approve/decline workflow\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/components/costs/CostEstimator.jsx`\n\n#### Task 3.3: Detailed Cost Analytics\n**Description**: Comprehensive cost breakdowns and analysis tools\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User can view costs by project, agent type, time period\n- Interactive charts for cost analysis (bar, pie, line charts)\n- Drill-down capability from overview to details\n- Export functionality for cost reports\n- Cost per token trends\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1, Task 3.2\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Files**: `src/components/costs/CostAnalytics.jsx`\n\n#### Task 3.4: Project Cost Attribution\n**Description**: Show costs attributed to specific projects and tasks\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees per-project cost breakdowns\n- Task-level cost attribution\n- Comparison of estimated vs actual costs\n- Project cost history and trends\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.3\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/components/costs/ProjectCosts.jsx`\n\n### Group 4: Agent Performance & Routing\n\n#### Task 4.1: Agent Performance Dashboard\n**Description**: Display agent success rates, performance metrics, and specialization data\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees agent performance comparison charts\n- Success rates by agent type and task complexity\n- Average execution times per agent\n- Agent specialization effectiveness metrics\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/components/agents/AgentPerformance.jsx`\n\n#### Task 4.2: Smart Routing Recommendations\n**Description**: Show agent routing recommendations with explanations\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees recommended agents for new tasks with reasoning\n- Comparison of agent suitability scores\n- Override capability for manual agent selection\n- Historical routing decisions and outcomes\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 4.1\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Files**: `src/components/agents/AgentRouter.jsx`\n\n### Group 5: Project Recovery Monitoring\n\n#### Task 5.1: Recovery Progress Tracker\n**Description**: Monitor and display progress of the 10 stalled project recoveries\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees list of projects being recovered with status\n- Progress indicators for each recovery attempt\n- Success/failure indicators with error details\n- Recovery timeline and milestones\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/components/recovery/RecoveryTracker.jsx`\n\n#### Task 5.2: Recovery Report Viewer\n**Description**: Display comprehensive recovery reports with outcomes\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User can view detailed recovery reports\n- Success/failure summary per project\n- Error analysis and resolution steps\n- Export capability for documentation\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 5.1\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Files**: `src/components/recovery/RecoveryReport.jsx`\n\n### Group 6: Real-time Data & API Integration\n\n#### Task 6.1: WebSocket Integration Service\n**Description**: Manage real-time connections for live metrics updates\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Real-time provider status updates\n- Live cost tracking during agent execution\n- Real-time project recovery progress\n- Proper connection management and reconnection logic\n\n**Dependencies**: None (foundational)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/services/websocketService.js`\n\n#### Task 6.2: Enhanced API Client\n**Description**: Extend API client for new endpoints (costs, providers, routing)\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- API calls for cost estimation and analytics\n- Provider management endpoints\n- Agent performance data retrieval\n- Recovery orchestration controls\n- Proper error handling and retry logic\n\n**Dependencies**: None (foundational)  \n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/services/apiClient.js`\n\n#### Task 6.3: Data State Management\n**Description**: Implement state management for new dashboard data types\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Centralized state for cost data, provider status, agent metrics\n- Efficient data caching and updates\n- State persistence for user preferences\n- Optimistic updates for better UX\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 6.1, Task 6.2\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Files**: `src/store/dashboardStore.js`, `src/hooks/useDashboardData.js`\n\n### Group 7: User Experience Enhancements\n\n#### Task 7.1: Interactive Chart Components\n**Description**: Reusable chart components for metrics visualization\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Line charts for trends (costs, performance over time)\n- Bar charts for comparisons (agent success rates)\n- Pie charts for distributions (cost by project)\n- Interactive features (hover, zoom, drill-down)\n- Consistent styling and responsive design\n\n**Dependencies**: None (foundational)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/components/charts/LineChart.jsx`, `src/components/charts/BarChart.jsx`, `src/components/charts/PieChart.jsx`\n\n#### Task 7.2: Advanced Filtering & Search\n**Description**: Filtering and search capabilities across all dashboard sections\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Date range filters for cost and performance data\n- Agent type and project filters\n- Search functionality for projects and agents\n- Filter persistence across sessions\n- Clear filter state management\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 7.1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/components/filters/FilterControls.jsx`, `src/hooks/useFilters.js`\n\n#### Task 7.3: Export & Reporting Tools\n**Description**: Allow users to export data and generate reports\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Export cost analytics to CSV/PDF\n- Generate printable performance reports\n- Schedule automated report generation\n- Email report delivery options\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 7.2\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Files**: `src/components/export/ExportTools.jsx`, `src/services/reportService.js`\n\n### Group 8: Mobile Optimization & Responsive Design\n\n#### Task 8.1: Mobile Dashboard Layout\n**Description**: Optimize dashboard for mobile and tablet viewing\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All dashboard sections accessible on mobile\n- Touch-friendly interactions\n- Collapsible sections for space efficiency\n- Proper chart scaling on small screens\n\n**Dependencies**: All UI components completed\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: `src/styles/mobile.css`, Updates to all component files\n\n#### Task 8.2: Progressive Web App Features\n**Description**: Add PWA capabilities for better mobile experience\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Offline viewing of cached dashboard data\n- Push notifications for cost alerts and recovery updates\n- Home screen installation capability\n- Background sync for metrics\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 8.1\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Files**: `public/manifest.json`, `src/sw.js`, PWA service files\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Week 1)\n- Task 1.1: Enhanced Dashboard Layout\n- Task 1.2: Navigation Enhancement  \n- Task 6.1: WebSocket Integration Service\n- Task 6.2: Enhanced API Client\n\n### Phase 2: Core Features (Week 2)\n- Task 2.1: Provider Status Dashboard\n- Task 3.1: Cost Overview Widget\n- Task 4.1: Agent Performance Dashboard\n- Task 5.1: Recovery Progress Tracker\n\n### Phase 3: Advanced Analytics (Week 3)\n- Task 2.2: Provider Performance Metrics\n- Task 3.3: Detailed Cost Analytics\n- Task 4.2: Smart Routing Recommendations\n- Task 7.1: Interactive Chart Components\n\n### Phase 4: Enhanced UX (Week 4)\n- Task 3.2: Pre-Execution Cost Estimator\n- Task 3.4: Project Cost Attribution\n- Task 5.2: Recovery Report Viewer\n- Task 6.3: Data State Management\n\n### Phase 5: Polish & Optimization (Week 5)\n- Task 7.2: Advanced Filtering & Search\n- Task 7.3: Export & Reporting Tools\n- Task 8.1: Mobile Dashboard Layout\n- Task 8.2: Progressive Web App Features\n\n## Technical Dependencies\n\n### External Libraries Required\n- Chart.js or Recharts for visualizations\n- date-fns for date manipulation\n- file-saver for export functionality\n- socket.io-client for WebSocket connections\n\n### API Endpoints Needed\n- `/api/providers/status` - Provider availability and health\n- `/api/costs/estimate` - Pre-execution cost estimation\n- `/api/costs/analytics` - Historical cost data\n- `/api/agents/performance` - Agent metrics and routing data\n- `/api/recovery/status` - Project recovery progress\n- WebSocket endpoint for real-time updates\n\n### Data Models\n- Provider status and metrics\n- Cost estimates and actuals\n- Agent performance data\n- Project recovery state\n- User preferences and filters\n\n## Success Metrics\n- Dashboard loads within 2 seconds\n- Real-time updates with <1 second latency\n- Mobile responsive on all screen sizes\n- 95% component test coverage\n- Accessibility compliance (WCAG 2.1 AA)\n\n## Risk Considerations\n- **Real-time data volume**: May need data sampling for performance\n- **Chart rendering performance**: Implement virtualization for large datasets\n- **Mobile performance**: Progressive loading and data pagination\n- **WebSocket reliability**: Implement robust reconnection logic\n\n---\n\n**Total Tasks**: 24 tasks across 8 groups\n**Estimated Duration**: 5 weeks\n**Complexity Distribution**: \n- Simple: 3 tasks\n- Medium: 15 tasks  \n- Complex: 6 tasks'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CxnUeZQ4RFgY3Sb45czHQB', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1_20260116_030224.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1_20260116_030224.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.3%\n- Average iterations per task: 4.3\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
