t handlers in `/src/ensemble/main.py`\n- Add event emission points throughout agent execution lifecycle\n- Implement progress state management\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 2: Automatic Error Recovery & Context Preservation\n**Duration**: 3-4 days  \n**Priority**: HIGH  \n**Phase**: Reliability Enhancement\n\n### Objective\nImplement intelligent error recovery with automatic retries and full context preservation for resume after failures.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Complete state manager resume functionality (message reconstruction)\n2. Retry logic with exponential backoff for transient failures\n3. Context preservation for spawned agents (parent context + partial results)\n4. Automatic checkpoint validation and rollback\n5. Error classification system (retryable vs. fatal)\n6. Tool execution result preservation across retries\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ Agents can resume from last checkpoint after crashes\n- ✅ Transient API errors trigger automatic retry\n- ✅ Failed spawns preserve parent agent state for debugging\n- ✅ Context includes: conversation history, tool results, spawned agent data\n- ✅ Recovery success rate > 80% for retryable errors\n- ✅ Zero token waste on successful recovery\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestone 1 (progress monitoring for recovery status)\n\n### Technical Focus\n- Complete `/src/ensemble/state.py` StateManager resume functionality\n- Enhance `/src/ensemble/runtime.py` with retry logic\n- Add error classification and recovery strategies\n- Implement checkpoint validation system\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 3: Agent Performance Analytics & Adaptive Optimization\n**Duration**: 2-3 days  \n**Priority**: MEDIUM  \n**Phase**: Optimization & Intelligence\n\n### Objective\nImplement comprehensive analytics tracking with adaptive model selection based on historical success rates.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Agent metrics tracking system (token usage, execution time, success rates)\n2. Aggregated metrics by agent type and model tier\n3. Analytics dashboard endpoint for reporting\n4. Adaptive model selection implementation\n5. Performance comparison reports (model A vs B)\n6. Metrics export functionality (JSON, CSV)\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ All agent executions tracked with complete metrics\n- ✅ Analytics API returns per-agent and aggregate statistics\n- ✅ Adaptive model selection improves success rate by 15%+\n- ✅ Token usage optimization reduces costs by 10%+\n- ✅ Reports identify underperforming agents for refinement\n- ✅ Metrics persist across system restarts\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestone 1 (progress data for metrics)\n- Milestone 2 (recovery data for success rates)\n\n### Technical Focus\n- Create new `AgentAnalytics` module\n- Add metrics collection throughout agent lifecycle\n- Implement adaptive model selection logic\n- Build analytics API endpoints\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 4: Testing, Documentation & Integration\n**Duration**: 1-2 days  \n**Priority**: HIGH  \n**Phase**: Quality Assurance\n\n### Objective\nComplete comprehensive testing, update documentation, and ensure seamless integration of all improvements.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Test suite covering all new functionality\n2. Performance benchmarks (before/after comparison)\n3. Updated documentation (README, implementation guide)\n4. Integration testing across all three improvements\n5. Final system validation and optimization\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ 100% test coverage for new functionality\n- ✅ All existing tests continue to pass\n- ✅ Performance benchmarks show improvement\n- ✅ Documentation accurately reflects new capabilities\n- ✅ System ready for production deployment\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestones 1, 2, 3 (all improvements implemented)\n\n### Technical Focus\n- Comprehensive testing across all modules\n- Performance validation and optimization\n- Documentation updates and examples\n- Final integration testing\n\n---\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n\n### High Risk Items\n1. **API Rate Limits**: Implement proper backoff and retry logic\n2. **State Corruption**: Add validation and rollback mechanisms  \n3. **Performance Regression**: Continuous monitoring during development\n4. **Backward Compatibility**: Maintain existing agent definition format\n\n### Mitigation Strategies\n- Incremental implementation with rollback capability\n- Extensive testing at each milestone\n- Performance monitoring throughout development\n- Staged deployment approach\n\n---\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n### User Experience\n- Real-time progress visibility (Milestone 1)\n- Reduced failure rates through recovery (Milestone 2)\n- Improved system performance through optimization (Milestone 3)\n\n### Technical Metrics  \n- Error recovery success rate > 80%\n- Progress update latency < 500ms\n- Token usage optimization > 10% cost reduction\n- Agent success rate improvement > 15%\n\n### Quality Assurance\n- Zero breaking changes to existing functionality\n- 100% test coverage for new features\n- Performance overhead < 5%\n- Documentation completeness score > 95%\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Begin Milestone 1: Progress Streaming implementation\n2. Set up development environment and testing framework\n3. Start with AgentRuntime enhancement for event emission\n4. Implement WebSocket streaming for progress updates'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012XmvY3pMZ2uq3HKQcEbDjN', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_025842.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_025842.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011BSJpgVDfxbwxE7gL3o18r', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ensemble_system_analysis_requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'focus': 'Analyze current ensemble system architecture and design architecture for the top 3 improvements: real-time progress streaming, error recovery & context preservation, and performance analytics with adaptive optimization'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011BSJpgVDfxbwxE7gL3o18r', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01X11agidW51GNGXbeiEdE2j', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ensemble_system_analysis_requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'focus': 'Analyze current ensemble system architecture and design architecture for the top 3 improvements: real-time progress streaming, error recovery & context preservation, and performance analytics with adaptive optimization'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01X11agidW51GNGXbeiEdE2j', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Comprehensive architecture proposal for ensemble agent system improvements, focusing on real-time progress streaming, error recovery, and performance analytics", "key_decisions": ["Adopt layered microservices architecture with event-driven communication", "Use FastAPI + asyncio for high-performance backend", "Implement Redis for state management and distributed caching", "Design three core improvement components: Progress Streaming, Error Recovery, Agent Analytics", "Use Kubernetes for scalable deployment with blue-green updates"], "self_analysis": "The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a comprehensive, modular approach to system improvements. By focusing on observability, adaptive intelligence, and minimal performance overhead, the design creates a robust framework for enhancing the ensemble agent system. The layered architecture allows for incremental implementation and future extensibility."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01A5qduKvHqBVjjAqDYbLoJv', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01A5qduKvHqBVjjAqDYbLoJv', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble UI Enhancements - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern: Feature-Driven Modular React Architecture\\nThe proposed architecture maintains the existing React + Bootstrap framework while introducing modular, composable components that enhance the user interface with new features.\\n\\n**Key Architectural Goals:**\\n- Minimal invasiveness to existing codebase\\n- High modularity and reusability\\n- Maintainable and testable component structure\\n- Performance optimization\\n- Responsive design preservation\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React (Existing)\\n- **Styling**: React-Bootstrap\\n- **State Management**: React Hooks (useState, useContext)\\n- **Utility Libraries**: \\n  - `lodash` for text processing\\n  - `react-intersection-observer` for scrolling/visibility features\\n\\n### Development Tools\\n- **Testing**: Jest, React Testing Library\\n- **Linting**: ESLint\\n- **Code Formatting**: Prettier\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### 1. AgentHierarchyTree (Enhanced)\\n**Responsibilities:**\\n- Render agent hierarchies\\n- Add question linking\\n- Generate and display two-word summaries\\n- Support collapsible/expandable views\\n\\n### 2. CompletedItemsSection (New Component)\\n**Responsibilities:**\\n- Manage and display completed tasks/agents\\n- Provide toggle for showing/hiding completed items\\n- Maintain completed items count\\n\\n### 3. MetricsPane (New Component)\\n**Responsibilities:**\\n- Display model usage metrics\\n- Show code delta information\\n- Real-time updates via polling mechanism\\n\\n### 4. Layout Manager\\n**Responsibilities:**\\n- Implement responsive grid adjustments\\n- Manage column width redistributions\\n- Handle section collapsibility\\n\\n## D. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AgentHierarchyTree/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 index.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 QuestionLink.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 SummaryGenerator.js\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 CompletedItemsSection/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MetricsPane/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 common/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 CollapsibleSection.jsx\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ResponsiveGrid.jsx\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 api.js         # Existing API service\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 metricsService.js  # New metrics data fetching\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 textProcessing.js  # Summary generation utilities\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 App.jsx\\n```\\n\\n## E. Data Flow & State Management\\n\\n### State Propagation\\n- Use React Context for global state management\\n- Lightweight hooks-based approach\\n- Polling mechanism integrated into services\\n\\n### Data Fetching Strategy\\n- Maintain existing 500ms-2s polling interval\\n- Add new `/api/metrics` endpoint handler\\n- Implement defensive error handling\\n\\n## F. API Design\\n\\n### New Metrics Endpoint\\n```json\\nGET /api/metrics\\nResponse: {\\n  \\"models\\": {\\n    \\"haiku\\": 5,\\n    \\"sonnet\\": 3,\\n    \\"opus\\": 1\\n  },\\n  \\"code_delta\\": {\\n    \\"lines_added\\": 245,\\n    \\"lines_removed\\": 89,\\n    \\"files_changed\\": 12\\n  },\\n  \\"last_updated\\": \\"2024-01-11T02:56:00Z\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## G. Deployment Strategy\\n- Existing React build process\\n- No changes to deployment pipeline\\n- Compatibility with current hosting infrastructure\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Component Testing\\n- Jest snapshot testing\\n- React Testing Library for interaction tests\\n- 90%+ code coverage goal\\n\\n### Testing Focus Areas\\n- Question link generation\\n- Metrics display accuracy\\n- Collapsible section behaviors\\n- Responsive layout rendering\\n\\n## I. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### 1. Performance Overhead\\n**Risk**: New components might slow rendering\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use React.memo\\n- Implement lazy loading\\n- Optimize polling intervals\\n\\n### 2. Browser Compatibility\\n**Risk**: New features might break in older browsers\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Test across modern browsers\\n- Provide graceful degradation\\n- Use well-supported React patterns\\n\\n## J. Open Questions for Stakeholder Review\\n1. Preferred method of question linking (scroll vs. navigate)\\n2. Desired default state for completed items section (collapsed/expanded)\\n3. Specific preferences for two-word summary generation algorithm\\n\\n## K. Implementation Phases\\n1. AgentHierarchyTree Enhancements\\n2. Completed Items Section\\n3. Metrics Pane\\n4. Layout Adjustments\\n5. Comprehensive Testing\\n\\n## Architecture Decision Record\\n- Maintained existing React + Bootstrap stack\\n- Chose modular, minimally invasive approach\\n- Prioritized