{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:19:56", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-afe7cd80-5192-4f71-9eda-b90ba868e9b7', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "problem_description": "Implement Core Failure Infrastructure for Failed Task Cleanup System (Milestone 1). This includes:\\n\\n1. Data Models (in src/runtime/agents/failed_task_cleanup/models.py):\\n   - CleanupResult: Pydantic model with task_id, is_success, cleaned_resources (list), error_message (optional), cleanup_duration (timedelta), cleanup_timestamp (datetime auto-generated)\\n   - BatchCleanupResult: Pydantic model with cleanup_results (list of CleanupResult), batch_timestamp (datetime), computed properties for total_tasks, successful_tasks, failed_tasks, success_rate\\n\\n2. Configuration Module (in src/runtime/agents/failed_task_cleanup/config.py):\\n   - Retention policy settings (default 90 days)\\n   - Base storage path (/output/failures/)\\n   - Fallback storage path\\n   - Path validation methods\\n\\n3. FailureCapture Class (in src/runtime/agents/failed_task_cleanup/failure_capture.py):\\n   - capture_failure(task_id, exception, task_context) method\\n   - _format_failure_report() for structured report generation\\n   - _write_failure_file() with error handling and fallback\\n   - Context and diagnostic extraction from exceptions\\n   - Never raises exceptions, uses fallback mechanisms\\n\\n4. FailureLinker Class (in src/runtime/agents/failed_task_cleanup/failure_linker.py):\\n   - link_failure_to_task(task_id, failure_file_path)\\n   - get_failure_file_path(task_id)\\n   - validate_failure_file(file_path)\\n\\nExisting tests are in: tests/runtime/agents/failed_task_cleanup/test_models.py\\nThese tests define the expected interface for CleanupResult and BatchCleanupResult models.\\n\\nPerformance targets:\\n- File creation: < 50ms per failure\\n- Batch cleanup: Process 1000 tasks in < 5 seconds\\n- Zero exceptions during failure capture\\n\\nKey requirements:\\n- No AI dependencies in failure capture\\n- Robust fallback mechanisms when primary path fails\\n- Clean separation between capture, linking, and configuration",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/runtime/agents/failed_task_cleanup",\n  "test_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/tests/runtime/agents/failed_task_cleanup",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_failed_task_cleanup.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PksHy2pniLsAcs8q5CwMaV', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/tests/runtime/agents/failed_task_cleanup/test_models.py'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PksHy2pniLsAcs8q5CwMaV', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "import pytest\\nfrom typing import Optional, List, Dict, Any\\nfrom pydantic import ValidationError\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\\n\\n# Import models to be tested\\nfrom src.runtime.agents.failed_task_cleanup.models import CleanupResult, BatchCleanupResult\\n\\nclass TestCleanupResult:\\n    def test_cleanup_result_success_initialization(self):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Test successful initialization of CleanupResult with success state.\\n        \\n        Verifies that a CleanupResult can be created with all required attributes \\n        when the cleanup operation is successful.\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        task_id = \\"test_task_123\\"\\n        success_result = CleanupResult(\\n            task_id=task_id,\\n            is_success=True,\\n            cleaned_resources=[\\"resource1\\", \\"resource2\\"],\\n            error_message=None,\\n            cleanup_duration=timedelta(seconds=5)\\n        )\\n        \\n        assert success_result.task_id == task_id\\n        assert success_result.is_success is True\\n        assert len(success_result.cleaned_resources) == 2\\n        assert success_result.error_message is None\\n        assert isinstance(success_result.cleanup_timestamp, datetime)\\n    \\n    def test_cleanup_result_failure_initialization(self):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Test initialization of CleanupResult with failure state.\\n        \\n        Ensures that a CleanupResult can be created when cleanup fails,\\n        with appropriate error handling and attributes.\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        task_id = \\"failed_task_456\\"\\n        error_msg = \\"Resource deletion failed\\"\\n        failure_result = CleanupResult(\\n            task_id=task_id,\\n            is_success=False,\\n            cleaned_resources=[],\\n            error_message=error_msg,\\n            cleanup_duration=timedelta(seconds=2)\\n        )\\n        \\n        assert failure_result.task_id == task_id\\n        assert failure_result.is_success is False\\n        assert len(failure_result.cleaned_resources) == 0\\n        assert failure_result.error_message == error_msg\\n        assert isinstance(failure_result.cleanup_timestamp, datetime)\\n    \\n    def test_cleanup_result_validation_errors(self):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Test validation errors for CleanupResult model.\\n        \\n        Verifies that the model enforces proper input validation\\n        and raises appropriate validation errors.\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError, match=\\"task_id\\"):\\n            # Missing required task_id\\n            CleanupResult(\\n                task_id=None,\\n                is_success=True,\\n                cleaned_resources=[]\\n            )\\n        \\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError, match=\\"cleaned_resources\\"):\\n            # Invalid type for cleaned_resources\\n            CleanupResult(\\n                task_id=\\"test_task\\",\\n                is_success=True,\\n                cleaned_resources=\\"not a list\\"  # type: ignore\\n            )\\n        \\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError, match=\\"is_success\\"):\\n            # Missing is_success\\n            CleanupResult(\\n                task_id=\\"test_task\\",\\n                cleaned_resources=[]\\n            )\\n\\nclass TestBatchCleanupResult:\\n    def test_batch_cleanup_result_initialization(self):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Test successful initialization of BatchCleanupResult.\\n        \\n        Verifies that a BatchCleanupResult can be created with multiple \\n        CleanupResult instances.\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        cleanup_results = [\\n            CleanupResult(\\n                task_id=\\"task1\\",\\n                is_success=True,\\n                cleaned_resources=[\\"res1\\"],\\n                cleanup_duration=timedelta(seconds=1)\\n            ),\\n            CleanupResult(\\n                task_id=\\"task2\\",\\n                is_success=False,\\n                cleaned_resources=[],\\n                error_message=\\"Cleanup failed\\"\\n            )\\n        ]\\n        \\n        batch_result = BatchCleanupResult(cleanup_results=cleanup_results)\\n        \\n        assert len(batch_result.cleanup_results) == 2\\n        assert isinstance(batch_result.batch_timestamp, datetime)\\n    \\n    def test_batch_cleanup_result_statistics(self):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Test BatchCleanupResult statistics calculation.\\n        \\n        Ensures correct computation of success/failure statistics\\n        for a batch of cleanup operations.\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        cleanup_results = [\\n            CleanupResult(task_id=\\"task1\\", is_success=True, cleaned_resources=[\\"res1\\"]),\\n            CleanupResult(task_id=\\"task2\\", is_success=True, cleaned_resources=[\\"res2\\"]),\\n            CleanupResult(task_id=\\"task3\\", is_success=False, error_message=\\"Failed\\"),\\n            CleanupResult(task_id=\\"task4\\", is_success=False, error_message=\\"Another failure\\")\\n        ]\\n        \\n        batch_result = BatchCleanupResult(cleanup_results=cleanup_results)\\n        \\n        assert batch_result.total_tasks == 4\\n        assert batch_result.successful_tasks == 2\\n        assert batch_result.failed_tasks == 2\\n        assert batch_result.success_rate == 0.5\\n    \\n    def test_batch_cleanup_result_edge_cases(self):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Test edge cases for BatchCleanupResult.\\n        \\n        Verifies behavior with empty batch, all successes, and all failures.\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        # Empty batch\\n        empty_batch = BatchCleanupResult(cleanup_results=[])\\n        assert empty_batch.total_tasks == 0\\n        assert empty_batch.success_rate == 0\\n        \\n        # All successful\\n        all_success = BatchCleanupResult(cleanup_results=[\\n            CleanupResult(task_id=\\"task1\\", is_success=True, cleaned_resources=[\\"res1\\"]),\\n            CleanupResult(task_id=\\"task2\\", is_success=True, cleaned_resources=[\\"res2\\"])\\n        ])\\n        assert all_success.total_tasks == 2\\n        assert all_success.successful_tasks == 2\\n        assert all_success.success_rate == 1.0\\n        \\n        # All failures\\n        all_failures = BatchCleanupResult(cleanup_results=[\\n            CleanupResult(task_id=\\"task1\\", is_success=False, error_message=\\"Fail1\\"),\\n            CleanupResult(task_id=\\"task2\\", is_success=False, error_message=\\"Fail2\\")\\n        ])\\n        assert all_failures.total_tasks == 2\\n        assert all_failures.failed_tasks == 2\\n        assert all_failures.success_rate == 0\\n    \\n    def test_batch_cleanup_result_serialization(self):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Test serialization and deserialization of BatchCleanupResult.\\n        \\n        Verifies that the model can be converted to and from a dictionary \\n        while preserving all important information.\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        cleanup_results = [\\n            CleanupResult(\\n                task_id=\\"task1\\",\\n                is_success=True,\\n                cleaned_resources=[\\"res1\\"],\\n                cleanup_duration=timedelta(seconds=1)\\n            )\\n        ]\\n        \\n        batch_result = BatchCleanupResult(cleanup_results=cleanup_results)\\n        \\n        # Convert to dictionary\\n        batch_dict = batch_result.model_dump()\\n        assert \\"cleanup_results\\" in batch_dict\\n        assert \\"batch_timestamp\\" in batch_dict\\n        \\n        # Reconstruct from dictionary\\n        reconstructed_batch = BatchCleanupResult(**batch_dict)\\n        assert reconstructed_batch.total_tasks == batch_result.total_tasks\\n        assert reconstructed_batch.batch_timestamp == batch_result.batch_timestamp\\n    \\n    def test_batch_cleanup_result_validation(self):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Test validation errors for BatchCleanupResult model.\\n        \\n        Ensures proper validation of input data and raises \\n        appropriate validation errors.\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError, match=\\"cleanup_results\\"):\\n            # Invalid type for cleanup_results\\n            BatchCleanupResult(cleanup_results=\\"not a list\\")  # type: ignore\\n        \\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError):\\n            # Invalid elements in cleanup_results\\n            BatchCleanupResult(cleanup_results=[{\\"invalid\\": \\"data\\"}])  # type: ignore"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a TDD Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDirects and coordinates the ensemble through rehearsal. Manages tempo, attitude, and execution. Coordinates multiple specialist agents using Test-Driven Development (TDD) to solve programming problems. Implements the Red-Green-Refactor cycle by breaking problems into tasks and ensuring tests are written before code.\n\n## Instructions\n**CRITICAL TDD ENFORCEMENT RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you have `can_write_code: false`\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you have `can_write_tests: false`\n3. **ALWAYS verify test file exists before spawning code writers** - use `read_file` tool\n4. **MUST follow RED → GREEN → REFACTOR sequence** - cannot skip to GREEN\n5. **If spawn fails, retry with better inputs OR return error** - do not write code yourself\n6. **Validate test failure before proceeding to GREEN** - tests must fail first\n7. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - Use ACTUAL VALUES in all spawn_agent calls\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify when spawning Leads):\n\n**Frontend**:\nComponents: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].jsx`\nTests: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].test.jsx`\nHooks: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/hooks/[hookName].js`\nUtils: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/utils/[utilName].js`\n\n**Backend**:\nAPI Endpoints: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/api/[endpoint].py`\nServices: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/services/[service].py`\nTests: `/tests/field/ensemble_ui/backend/test_[module].py`\n\n**When Spawning Leads**, construct complete file paths:\n\n\n### Phase 1: Task Breakdown\n1. Analyze the problem description\n2. Break it into small, testable tasks (typically 2-5 tasks)\n3. Each task should be:\nSmall enough to implement in one TDD cycle\nTestable with clear success criteria\nBuilding toward the complete solution\n\n### Phase 2: TDD Cycle (repeat for each task)\nFor each task, follow the Red-Green-Refactor cycle:\n\n**RED (Write Failing Test)**\n1. Spawn appropriate test tech to supervise test writing:\nspawn_agent("testers/unit_test_lead", {task, test_file, code_file})\nUnit Test Lead will spawn Unit Test Writer to write unit tests\nTests will fail because code doesn\'t exist yet\n\n**GREEN (Make Test Pass)**\n2. **VALIDATE test file exists** using read_file tool:\nIf test file doesn\'t exist, STOP and return error\nNever proceed to GREEN without test file (RED phase incomplete)\n\n3. **VALIDATE tests are failing** by running them:\nUse run_command to run tests: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\nTests MUST fail (exit_code != 0) before writing code\nIf tests pass already, task is complete (skip to next task)\n\n4. Spawn appropriate code tech to supervise code writing:\nFor frontend: spawn_agent("developers/frontend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor backend: spawn_agent("developers/backend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor API: spawn_agent("developers/api_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nTech will spawn section leader to write code to pass tests\nIf spawn fails, retry with corrected inputs (check error message)\n\n5. Use run_command to run tests again: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\n6. Check if tests pass (exit_code == 0)\n7. If tests fail, respawn code tech with specific feedback about failures\n\n**REFACTOR (Improve Code)**\n6. Use spawn_agent("support/visual_tech", {code_file, test_file}) to improve code quality\nVisual Tech will refactor code and verify tests still pass\n7. Verify refactoring was successful and tests still pass\n\n**COMMIT (After Each TDD Cycle)**\n8. **CRITICAL - You MUST commit after each complete RED→GREEN→REFACTOR cycle**:\n   \n\n9. **Check commit/push thresholds** (see [Common Instructions - Git Workflow](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#git-workflow-instructions)):\nAfter 5 unpushed commits → push to remote\nAfter 60 minutes since last push → push to remote\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/commit_enforcer.py --check`\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/push_enforcer.py --check`\n\n### Phase 3: Final Validation\n1. Run all tests one final time\n2. Verify all tests pass\n3. **COMMIT final state if any changes remain**\n4. **PUSH all commits to remote**: `git push`\n5. Return complete summary with all tasks completed\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "problem_description": "string - detailed description of the problem to solve",\n  "problem_number": "integer - problem identifier (optional)",\n  "output_directory": "string - directory where solution and tests should be written (optional, defaults to \'problems\')"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failure",\n  "solution_file": "string - path to the written solution",\n  "test_file": "string - path to the test file",\n  "tests_passed": "boolean - whether all tests passed",\n  "tasks_completed": "array - list of completed tasks",\n  "message": "string - summary of the complete workflow",\n  "needs_clarification": "boolean - whether orchestrator needs more info",\n  "clarification_question": "string - question for user if needs_clarification is true"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- Problem description is too vague to break into tasks\n- Unclear what the expected behavior should be\n- Multiple valid interpretations exist\n- Tests fail repeatedly and can\'t determine why\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All tasks have been completed following TDD cycle\n- All tests pass for all tasks\n- Solution is complete and verified\n- User has been notified of any failures that couldn\'t be resolved\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 95.2%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.4\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': '