{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:20:00", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-99f2fb83-431e-4eb2-b594-6d85d80fe395', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/architecture.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019HUN2G84ifkRuaoJ2baYqH', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'agent-cost-tracking-enhancement', 'description': 'Implement agent cost tracking enhancement features based on architecture document requirements'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019HUN2G84ifkRuaoJ2baYqH', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "dc4ddfd6", "message": "Created project: agent-cost-tracking-enhancement", "summary": {"project_id": "dc4ddfd6", "project_name": "agent-cost-tracking-enhancement", "description": "Implement agent cost tracking enhancement features based on architecture document requirements", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T03:19:03.858100", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T03:19:03.858100", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T03:19:03.858100", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'agent-cost-tracking-enhancement\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01V5iXrf1JEeSkkkq1Jaus48', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01V5iXrf1JEeSkkkq1Jaus48', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis document outlines the architecture for enhancing the ensemble UI to display cost estimates, execution duration, and model information for each agent task.\\n\\n## System Context\\n\\n### Current Architecture\\nThe system has:\\n- **Backend**: Activity tracking via `activity_tracker.py` that monitors agent execution\\n- **API Layer**: WebSocket/REST endpoints in `main.py` that expose agent state\\n- **Frontend**: React-based UI with `AgentSummaryPane.jsx` displaying agent information\\n- **Agent Runtime**: `AgentRuntime` managing agent execution with Claude API\\n\\n### Enhancement Goals\\nAdd cost and timing metrics to the existing activity tracking and display pipeline.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Component Architecture\\n\\n### 1. Backend Components\\n\\n#### 1.1 Activity Tracker Extension (`activity_tracker.py`)\\n**Current State**: Tracks agent lifecycle, tool usage, iterations, and status changes\\n\\n**Enhancements**:\\n- Extend `record_agent_started()` to capture:\\n  - `started_at`: ISO timestamp\\n  - `model_used`: Model identifier from AgentRuntime\\n- Extend `record_agent_completed()` to capture:\\n  - `completed_at`: ISO timestamp\\n  - `duration_ms`: Calculated duration in milliseconds\\n  - `cost_estimate`: Calculated cost in USD\\n  - `token_usage`: Input/output tokens used\\n\\n**Data Structure Changes**:\\n```python\\n# Enhanced agent_hierarchy entry\\n{\\n    \\"agent_id\\": str,\\n    \\"agent_name\\": str,\\n    \\"agent_type\\": str,\\n    \\"status\\": str,\\n    \\"started_at\\": str,  # ISO timestamp\\n    \\"completed_at\\": str,  # ISO timestamp (optional)\\n    \\"duration_ms\\": int,  # milliseconds (optional)\\n    \\"model_used\\": str,  # e.g., \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\"\\n    \\"cost_estimate\\": float,  # USD (optional)\\n    \\"token_usage\\": {  # optional\\n        \\"input_tokens\\": int,\\n        \\"output_tokens\\": int,\\n        \\"total_tokens\\": int\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n#### 1.2 Cost Calculator (New Module: `cost_calculator.py`)\\n**Purpose**: Calculate cost estimates based on token usage and model pricing\\n\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Maintain model pricing table (per-token costs)\\n- Calculate cost from token usage\\n- Handle different model families (Sonnet, Opus, Haiku)\\n- Provide estimation when exact token counts unavailable\\n\\n**Interface**:\\n```python\\nclass CostCalculator:\\n    def calculate_cost(\\n        self,\\n        model: str,\\n        input_tokens: int,\\n        output_tokens: int\\n    ) -> float:\\n        \\"\\"\\"Calculate cost in USD\\"\\"\\"\\n        pass\\n    \\n    def estimate_cost_from_chars(\\n        self,\\n        model: str,\\n        input_chars: int,\\n        output_chars: int\\n    ) -> float:\\n        \\"\\"\\"Estimate cost when token counts unavailable\\"\\"\\"\\n        pass\\n```\\n\\n**Model Pricing Table** (as of Jan 2024):\\n```python\\nMODEL_PRICING = {\\n    \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\": {\\n        \\"input\\": 0.003 / 1000,  # $3 per million tokens\\n        \\"output\\": 0.015 / 1000   # $15 per million tokens\\n    },\\n    \\"claude-3-opus-20240229\\": {\\n        \\"input\\": 0.015 / 1000,\\n        \\"output\\": 0.075 / 1000\\n    },\\n    \\"claude-3-haiku-20240307\\": {\\n        \\"input\\": 0.00025 / 1000,\\n        \\"output\\": 0.00125 / 1000\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n#### 1.3 AgentRuntime Integration\\n**Current State**: Manages agent execution, tracks iterations and tool use\\n\\n**Enhancements**:\\n- Capture start time on initialization\\n- Extract model identifier from configuration\\n- Extract token usage from Claude API responses\\n- Calculate cost using `CostCalculator`\\n- Pass metrics to `activity_tracker` on completion\\n\\n**Implementation Points**:\\n- In `__init__`: Record start time\\n- In `_process_response()`: Extract token usage from API response\\n- In completion/failure: Calculate duration and cost, pass to activity tracker\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. API Layer\\n\\n#### 2.1 WebSocket/REST Endpoints (`main.py`)\\n**Current State**: Provides endpoints for agent state and activity data\\n\\n**Enhancements**:\\n- Include new fields in agent state responses:\\n  - `started_at`, `completed_at`, `duration_ms`\\n  - `model_used`, `cost_estimate`, `token_usage`\\n- Ensure backward compatibility (new fields optional)\\n\\n**Response Format**:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"agent_id\\": \\"exec_dir_1\\",\\n  \\"agent_name\\": \\"Executive Director\\",\\n  \\"agent_type\\": \\"executive_director\\",\\n  \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n  \\"started_at\\": \\"2024-01-13T10:30:00.123Z\\",\\n  \\"completed_at\\": \\"2024-01-13T10:30:42.456Z\\",\\n  \\"duration_ms\\": 42333,\\n  \\"model_used\\": \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\",\\n  \\"cost_estimate\\": 0.0042,\\n  \\"token_usage\\": {\\n    \\"input_tokens\\": 1200,\\n    \\"output_tokens\\": 350,\\n    \\"total_tokens\\": 1550\\n  },\\n  \\"current_task\\": \\"Completed\\",\\n  \\"children\\": []\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Frontend Components\\n\\n#### 3.1 AgentSummaryPane Enhancement (`AgentSummaryPane.jsx`)\\n**Current State**: Displays agent name, type, status, current task\\n\\n**Enhancements**:\\nAdd display sections for:\\n1. **Execution Timeline**: Start \\u2192 End times (relative or absolute)\\n2. **Duration Badge**: Formatted duration (e.g., \\"2.3s\\", \\"1m 45s\\")\\n3. **Cost Badge**: Formatted cost (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n4. **Model Tag**: Shortened model name (e.g., \\"Sonnet 3.5\\")\\n\\n**Layout Design**:\\n```\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502 \\ud83e\\udd16 Executive Director                   \\u2502\\n\\u2502 Status: \\u2705 Completed                     \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                         \\u2502\\n\\u2502 \\u23f1\\ufe0f 2.3s  \\ud83d\\udcb0 $0.0042  \\ud83c\\udff7\\ufe0f Sonnet 3.5     \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                         \\u2502\\n\\u2502 Started: 10:30:00                       \\u2502\\n\\u2502 Completed: 10:30:02                     \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                         \\u2502\\n\\u2502 Current Task: Completed                 \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n```\\n\\n**Utility Functions**:\\n```javascript\\n// Format duration\\nfunction formatDuration(durationMs) {\\n  if (durationMs < 1000) return `${durationMs}ms`;\\n  if (durationMs < 60000) return `${(durationMs / 1000).toFixed(1)}s`;\\n  const mins = Math.floor(durationMs / 60000);\\n  const secs = ((durationMs % 60000) / 1000).toFixed(0);\\n  return `${mins}m ${secs}s`;\\n}\\n\\n// Format cost\\nfunction formatCost(costUsd) {\\n  if (costUsd === null || costUsd === undefined) return \'N/A\';\\n  if (costUsd < 0.0001) return \'<$0.0001\';\\n  return `$${costUsd.toFixed(4)}`;\\n}\\n\\n// Shorten model name\\nfunction formatModelName(model) {\\n  if (model.includes(\'sonnet\')) return \'Sonnet 3.5\';\\n  if (model.includes(\'opus\')) return \'Opus\';\\n  if (model.includes(\'haiku\')) return \'Haiku\';\\n  return model;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n### 1. Agent Execution Start\\n```\\nAgentRuntime.__init__()\\n  \\u2193\\nRecord start_time\\n  \\u2193\\nactivity_tracker.record_agent_started(\\n  agent_id, agent_name, agent_type, model_used, started_at\\n)\\n  \\u2193\\nUpdate agent_hierarchy and agent_states\\n  \\u2193\\nEmit to WebSocket\\n  \\u2193\\nFrontend receives agent state\\n  \\u2193\\nAgentSummaryPane displays \\"Running\\" with start time\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Agent Execution Completion\\n```\\nAgentRuntime completes\\n  \\u2193\\nExtract token_usage from API response\\n  \\u2193\\nCalculate duration_ms = now - start_time\\n  \\u2193\\nCostCalculator.calculate_cost(model, tokens)\\n  \\u2193\\nactivity_tracker.record_agent_completed(\\n  agent_id, completed_at, duration_ms, cost_estimate, token_usage\\n)\\n  \\u2193\\nUpdate agent_hierarchy and agent_states\\n  \\u2193\\nEmit to WebSocket\\n  \\u2193\\nFrontend receives updated agent state\\n  \\u2193\\nAgentSummaryPane displays metrics badges\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technology Stack\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python 3.11+\\n- **Framework**: Existing activity_tracker system\\n- **API**: WebSocket/REST (existing)\\n- **New Module**: `cost_calculator.py`\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React\\n- **Component**: `AgentSummaryPane.jsx`\\n- **Styling**: Existing CSS/styling system\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Design Decisions\\n\\n### 1. Cost Calculation Strategy\\n**Decision**: Calculate cost at agent completion time\\n**Rationale**: \\n- Token counts only available after API response\\n- Avoids streaming cost updates (complexity)\\n- Matches milestone scope (show on completion)\\n\\n### 2. Token Usage Source\\n**Decision**: Extract from Claude API response `usage` field\\n**Rationale**:\\n- Most accurate source\\n- Already available in API responses\\n- Fallback to estimation if unavailable\\n\\n### 3. Model Pricing Storage\\n**Decision**: Hardcode pricing in `cost_calculator.py`\\n**Rationale**:\\n- Pricing changes infrequently\\n- Simple to update\\n- Future: Could load from config file\\n\\n### 4. Duration Precision\\n**Decision**: Store in milliseconds, display with appropriate units\\n**Rationale**:\\n- Milliseconds provide precision\\n- Display formatting adapts to duration length\\n- Easy to aggregate for analytics later\\n\\n### 5. Backward Compatibility\\n**Decision**: All new fields optional in API responses\\n**Rationale**:\\n- Existing consumers won\'t break\\n- Graceful degradation if data missing\\n- Frontend checks for field existence\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Cost calculation: < 1ms per agent\\n- No impact on agent execution speed\\n- Activity tracker overhead: < 5% of execution time\\n\\n### Reliability\\n- Handle missing token usage gracefully\\n- Fallback to estimation when needed\\n- Never crash agent execution due to tracking failures\\n\\n### Maintainability\\n- Model pricing centralized and easy to update\\n- Clear separation of concerns (tracking, calculation, display)\\n- Well-documented data structures\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Tests\\n1. **CostCalculator**:\\n   - Test cost calculation for each model\\n   - Test estimation fallback\\n   - Test edge cases (zero tokens, unknown model)\\n\\n2. **ActivityTracker**:\\n   - Test new fields captured correctly\\n   - Test backward compatibility\\n   - Test data structure updates\\n\\n### Integration Tests\\n1. **End-to-End Flow**:\\n   - Agent execution \\u2192 cost calculation \\u2192 API \\u2192 Frontend\\n   - Verify metrics display correctly\\n   - Test with different models\\n\\n2. **API Tests**:\\n   - Verify new fields in responses\\n   - Test backward compatibility\\n   - Test WebSocket updates\\n\\n### Frontend Tests\\n1. **Component Tests**:\\n   - Test duration formatting\\n   - Test cost formatting\\n   - Test model name shortening\\n   - Test missing data handling\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Security Considerations\\n\\n### Data Privacy\\n- Cost data not sensitive but could reveal usage patterns\\n- No additional authentication required (existing auth applies)\\n\\n### Input Validation\\n- Validate token counts are non-negative\\n- Validate duration is non-negative\\n- Handle malformed model names gracefully\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Phase 1: Backend (Milestone 1)\\n- Deploy `cost_calculator.py`\\n- Update `activity_tracker.py`\\n- Update `AgentRuntime` integration\\n- Test with existing agents\\n\\n### Phase 2: API (Milestone 2)\\n- Update API responses\\n- Test backward compatibility\\n- Deploy to staging\\n\\n### Phase 3: Frontend (Milestone 3)\\n- Update `AgentSummaryPane.jsx`\\n- Test display formatting\\n- Deploy to production\\n\\n### Rollback Plan\\n- Backend changes backward compatible\\n- Frontend can gracefully handle missing fields\\n- Can rollback each phase independently\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Future Enhancements\\n\\n### Out of Current Scope\\n1. **Historical Analytics**:\\n   - Cost aggregation by agent type\\n   - Cost trends over time\\n   - Budget tracking\\n\\n2. **Budget Controls**:\\n   - Alert when cost exceeds threshold\\n   - Pause execution on budget limit\\n   - Per-project cost limits\\n\\n3. **Detailed Breakdown**:\\n   - Per-tool cost attribution\\n   - Cost by iteration\\n   - Cost heatmaps\\n\\n4. **Real-Time Streaming**:\\n   - Stream cost updates during execution\\n   - Live token counting\\n   - Incremental cost display\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Appendix\\n\\n### A. File Locations\\n- Backend: `/src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\\n- New Module: `/src/runtime/agents/cost_calculator.py`\\n- AgentRuntime: `/src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` (or similar)\\n- API: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/main.py`\\n- Frontend: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AgentSummaryPane.jsx`\\n\\n### B. Model Pricing Reference\\nUpdated pricing at: https://www.anthropic.com/pricing\\n\\n### C. Claude API Token Usage Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"usage\\": {\\n    \\"input_tokens\\": 1200,\\n    \\"output_tokens\\": 350\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TxvDcnTqh1Ne4G5vMPB9pR', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': '# Requirements: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\n\n## Project Vision\nEnhance the ensemble UI to display cost estimates, execution duration, and model information for each agent task, enabling users to understand the resource consumption and performance characteristics of their AI workflows.\n\n## Problem Statement\nCurrently, the ensemble UI shows agent execution status and basic information, but provides no visibility into:\n- Cost incurred by each agent\'s API usage\n- Time taken for agent execution\n- Which AI model was used\n- Token consumption patterns\n\nThis lack of visibility makes it difficult for users to optimize workflows, understand resource consumption, or budget for AI operations.\n\n## Solution Overview\nAdd comprehensive cost and performance tracking to the existing activity tracking and display pipeline:\n\n1. **Backend Enhancement**: Extend activity tracking to capture timing, cost, and model usage\n2. **Cost Calculation**: Implement cost calculator with current model pricing\n3. **API Extension**: Include new metrics in existing endpoints\n4. **UI Enhancement**: Display cost, duration, and model badges in agent summary panes\n\n## Objectives\n\n### Primary Objectives\n1. **Display Agent Costs**: Show cost estimate for each completed agent\n2. **Show Execution Duration**: Display formatted execution time for each agent\n3. **Display Model Information**: Show which AI model was used per agent\n4. **Maintain Performance**: No impact on agent execution speed\n5. **Preserve Compatibility**: All enhancements backward compatible\n\n### Secondary Objectives\n1. **Accurate Metrics**: Use actual token usage when available\n2. **Graceful Degradation**: Handle missing data appropriately\n3. **Clear Display**: Intuitive formatting of cost and duration\n4. **Real-time Updates**: Metrics appear as soon as agent completes\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR1: Cost Tracking\n- **FR1.1**: Calculate cost based on actual token usage from Claude API\n- **FR1.2**: Support Claude 3.5 Sonnet, Opus, and Haiku models\n- **FR1.3**: Display cost in USD with appropriate precision\n- **FR1.4**: Handle cases where token usage unavailable (estimation fallback)\n\n### FR2: Duration Tracking\n- **FR2.1**: Track agent start and completion times\n- **FR2.2**: Calculate duration in milliseconds\n- **FR2.3**: Display duration with appropriate units (ms, s, m s)\n- **FR2.4**: Show execution timeline in agent summary\n\n### FR3: Model Information\n- **FR3.1**: Capture model identifier from agent runtime\n- **FR3.2**: Display shortened model name (e.g., "Sonnet 3.5")\n- **FR3.3**: Associate model with specific agent execution\n\n### FR4: Data Integration\n- **FR4.1**: Extend activity tracker to capture new metrics\n- **FR4.2**: Include metrics in WebSocket/REST API responses\n- **FR4.3**: Update agent hierarchy data structure\n- **FR4.4**: Maintain existing API contract (new fields optional)\n\n### FR5: UI Display\n- **FR5.1**: Add cost badge to AgentSummaryPane\n- **FR5.2**: Add duration badge to AgentSummaryPane\n- **FR5.3**: Add model tag to AgentSummaryPane\n- **FR5.4**: Show start/completion times\n- **FR5.5**: Handle missing metrics gracefully\n\n## Technical Requirements\n\n### TR1: Backend Components\n- **TR1.1**: Create `CostCalculator` class with model pricing table\n- **TR1.2**: Extend `ActivityTracker` to capture timing and cost data\n- **TR1.3**: Integrate with `AgentRuntime` to extract metrics\n- **TR1.4**: Update API endpoints to include new fields\n\n### TR2: Data Structure\n```python\n# Enhanced agent data structure\n{\n    "agent_id": str,\n    "agent_name": str,\n    "agent_type": str,\n    "status": str,\n    "started_at": str,  # ISO timestamp\n    "completed_at": str,  # ISO timestamp (optional)\n    "duration_ms": int,  # milliseconds (optional)\n    "model_used": str,  # e.g., "claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022"\n    "cost_estimate": float,  # USD (optional)\n    "token_usage": {  # optional\n        "input_tokens": int,\n        "output_tokens": int,\n        "total_tokens": int\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### TR3: Model Pricing\nCurrent Claude pricing (January 2024):\n- **Claude 3.5 Sonnet**: $3/million input, $15/million output\n- **Claude 3 Opus**: $15/million input, $75/million output\n- **Claude 3 Haiku**: $0.25/million input, $1.25/million output\n\n### TR4: Frontend Components\n- **TR4.1**: Update `AgentSummaryPane.jsx` with new display elements\n- **TR4.2**: Implement formatting utilities for cost/duration\n- **TR4.3**: Add appropriate icons/styling for metrics\n- **TR4.4**: Ensure responsive layout\n\n## User Stories\n\n### US1: Cost Visibility\n**As a** user running AI workflows  \n**I want to** see the cost of each agent execution  \n**So that** I can understand and optimize my AI spending\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Cost displayed as badge in agent summary (e.g., "$0.0042")\n- Cost calculated from actual token usage when available\n- Cost appears when agent completes\n- Cost shows appropriate precision (4 decimal places for small amounts)\n\n### US2: Performance Monitoring\n**As a** user debugging workflows  \n**I want to** see how long each agent takes to execute  \n**So that** I can identify performance bottlenecks\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Duration displayed as badge in agent summary (e.g., "2.3s")\n- Duration shows from agent start to completion\n- Duration formatted appropriately (ms for <1s, s for <1min, m s for longer)\n- Start/completion times visible in summary\n\n### US3: Model Transparency\n**As a** user optimizing workflows  \n**I want to** see which AI model each agent used  \n**So that** I can understand model selection and costs\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Model displayed as tag in agent summary (e.g., "Sonnet 3.5")\n- Model name shortened for readability\n- Model associated with specific agent execution\n- Model information persists after completion\n\n### US4: Real-time Updates\n**As a** user monitoring live workflows  \n**I want to** see metrics appear as agents complete  \n**So that** I can track progress and costs in real-time\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Start time appears when agent begins\n- Metrics appear when agent completes\n- UI updates via WebSocket without page refresh\n- No visible delays in metric display\n\n## Constraints\n\n### Technical Constraints\n- **TC1**: Must not impact agent execution performance\n- **TC2**: Must maintain backward compatibility with existing API consumers\n- **TC3**: Must handle network failures gracefully during metric collection\n- **TC4**: Must use existing authentication and authorization mechanisms\n\n### Business Constraints\n- **BC1**: Model pricing hardcoded initially (updatable in future)\n- **BC2**: No budget controls or alerting in initial version\n- **BC3**: No historical analytics or cost aggregation\n- **BC4**: Focus on individual agent metrics only\n\n### Technology Constraints\n- **TK1**: Use existing Python backend and React frontend\n- **TK2**: Leverage existing activity tracking infrastructure\n- **TK3**: Follow existing UI design patterns and styling\n- **TK4**: Use Claude API token usage data as primary source\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### User Acceptance\n1. **Cost Visibility**: Users can see cost for 95% of completed agents\n2. **Duration Accuracy**: Duration displayed within 100ms of actual execution time\n3. **Model Information**: Model name visible for all agents\n4. **Performance Impact**: < 5% overhead added to agent execution time\n5. **UI Responsiveness**: Metrics appear within 1 second of agent completion\n\n### Technical Acceptance\n1. **API Compatibility**: Existing API consumers continue working without changes\n2. **Error Handling**: System gracefully handles missing or invalid metric data\n3. **Test Coverage**: 90% test coverage for new components\n4. **Documentation**: All new APIs and components documented\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n### Current Version\n- **Historical cost analytics and reporting**\n- **Budget controls and alerting**\n- **Cost breakdown by tool or iteration**\n- **Real-time streaming cost updates during execution**\n- **Cost aggregation across multiple agents**\n- **External cost tracking integrations**\n- **Cost optimization recommendations**\n\n### Future Considerations\n- Integration with external budget tracking systems\n- Advanced cost analytics and visualizations\n- Predictive cost modeling\n- Multi-cloud cost tracking\n- Cost alerts and budget controls\n\n## Assumptions\n\n### Technical Assumptions\n- Claude API responses include `usage` field with token counts\n- Activity tracker can be extended without breaking existing functionality\n- WebSocket connections remain stable for real-time updates\n- Agent runtime provides access to model configuration\n\n### Business Assumptions\n- Current model pricing remains stable during implementation\n- Users primarily interested in per-agent costs vs. aggregate costs\n- Cost precision to 4 decimal places sufficient for user needs\n- Duration tracking in milliseconds adequate for performance analysis\n\n### User Assumptions\n- Users understand AI model cost concepts\n- Users can interpret duration and cost metrics effectively\n- Users will use cost information for workflow optimization\n- Users prioritize accuracy over real-time streaming updates\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Internal Dependencies\n- Activity Tracker system (`activity_tracker.py`)\n- Agent Runtime system\n- WebSocket/API infrastructure (`main.py`)\n- AgentSummaryPane component\n- Existing authentication/authorization\n\n### External Dependencies\n- Claude API with consistent token usage reporting\n- React framework for frontend updates\n- Python 3.11+ for backend enhancements\n- Existing build and deployment pipeline\n\n## Implementation Approach\n\n### Development Methodology\n- **Test-Driven Development (TDD)**: Write tests first, then implementation\n- **Incremental Delivery**: Backend → API → Frontend phases\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Ensure existing functionality unaffected\n- **Performance Monitoring**: Track impact on execution speed\n\n### Testing Strategy\n1. **Unit Tests**: Cost calculation, formatting utilities, data structures\n2. **Integration Tests**: End-to-end flow from agent execution to UI display\n3. **API Tests**: Response format validation and backward compatibility\n4. **Frontend Tests**: Component rendering and data handling\n5. **Performance Tests**: Execution overhead measurement\n\n### Risk Mitigation\n- **Missing Token Data**: Fallback to estimation based on character counts\n- **API Changes**: Defensive programming for token usage field changes\n- **Performance Impact**: Asynchronous processing where possible\n- **UI Compatibility**: Progressive enhancement with feature detection\n\nThis requirements document provides the foundation for implementing agent cost tracking enhancement using test-driven development methodology.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TxvDcnTqh1Ne4G5vMPB9pR', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260116_032000.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260116_032000.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n  "user_question": "string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 75.7%\n- Average iterations per task: 14.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, NotFoundError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Quickly identifying the specific file needing modification through targeted searches, 3) Recognizing th...\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Conducting systematic directory analysis using multiple commands to gather comprehensive data, 3) Creat...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
