{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:20:17", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f40b6135-efd3-4491-a04a-284b90ecfa15', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "agent-cost-tracking-enhancement"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01ERjjCQE9ptCQvTH53KK2vs', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01ERjjCQE9ptCQvTH53KK2vs', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nEnhance the ensemble UI to display cost estimates, execution duration, and model information for each agent task, enabling users to understand the resource consumption and performance characteristics of their AI workflows.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nCurrently, the ensemble UI shows agent execution status and basic information, but provides no visibility into:\\n- Cost incurred by each agent\'s API usage\\n- Time taken for agent execution\\n- Which AI model was used\\n- Token consumption patterns\\n\\nThis lack of visibility makes it difficult for users to optimize workflows, understand resource consumption, or budget for AI operations.\\n\\n## Solution Overview\\nAdd comprehensive cost and performance tracking to the existing activity tracking and display pipeline:\\n\\n1. **Backend Enhancement**: Extend activity tracking to capture timing, cost, and model usage\\n2. **Cost Calculation**: Implement cost calculator with current model pricing\\n3. **API Extension**: Include new metrics in existing endpoints\\n4. **UI Enhancement**: Display cost, duration, and model badges in agent summary panes\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Objectives\\n1. **Display Agent Costs**: Show cost estimate for each completed agent\\n2. **Show Execution Duration**: Display formatted execution time for each agent\\n3. **Display Model Information**: Show which AI model was used per agent\\n4. **Maintain Performance**: No impact on agent execution speed\\n5. **Preserve Compatibility**: All enhancements backward compatible\\n\\n### Secondary Objectives\\n1. **Accurate Metrics**: Use actual token usage when available\\n2. **Graceful Degradation**: Handle missing data appropriately\\n3. **Clear Display**: Intuitive formatting of cost and duration\\n4. **Real-time Updates**: Metrics appear as soon as agent completes\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR1: Cost Tracking\\n- **FR1.1**: Calculate cost based on actual token usage from Claude API\\n- **FR1.2**: Support Claude 3.5 Sonnet, Opus, and Haiku models\\n- **FR1.3**: Display cost in USD with appropriate precision\\n- **FR1.4**: Handle cases where token usage unavailable (estimation fallback)\\n\\n### FR2: Duration Tracking\\n- **FR2.1**: Track agent start and completion times\\n- **FR2.2**: Calculate duration in milliseconds\\n- **FR2.3**: Display duration with appropriate units (ms, s, m s)\\n- **FR2.4**: Show execution timeline in agent summary\\n\\n### FR3: Model Information\\n- **FR3.1**: Capture model identifier from agent runtime\\n- **FR3.2**: Display shortened model name (e.g., \\"Sonnet 3.5\\")\\n- **FR3.3**: Associate model with specific agent execution\\n\\n### FR4: Data Integration\\n- **FR4.1**: Extend activity tracker to capture new metrics\\n- **FR4.2**: Include metrics in WebSocket/REST API responses\\n- **FR4.3**: Update agent hierarchy data structure\\n- **FR4.4**: Maintain existing API contract (new fields optional)\\n\\n### FR5: UI Display\\n- **FR5.1**: Add cost badge to AgentSummaryPane\\n- **FR5.2**: Add duration badge to AgentSummaryPane\\n- **FR5.3**: Add model tag to AgentSummaryPane\\n- **FR5.4**: Show start/completion times\\n- **FR5.5**: Handle missing metrics gracefully\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### TR1: Backend Components\\n- **TR1.1**: Create `CostCalculator` class with model pricing table\\n- **TR1.2**: Extend `ActivityTracker` to capture timing and cost data\\n- **TR1.3**: Integrate with `AgentRuntime` to extract metrics\\n- **TR1.4**: Update API endpoints to include new fields\\n\\n### TR2: Data Structure\\n```python\\n# Enhanced agent data structure\\n{\\n    \\"agent_id\\": str,\\n    \\"agent_name\\": str,\\n    \\"agent_type\\": str,\\n    \\"status\\": str,\\n    \\"started_at\\": str,  # ISO timestamp\\n    \\"completed_at\\": str,  # ISO timestamp (optional)\\n    \\"duration_ms\\": int,  # milliseconds (optional)\\n    \\"model_used\\": str,  # e.g., \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\"\\n    \\"cost_estimate\\": float,  # USD (optional)\\n    \\"token_usage\\": {  # optional\\n        \\"input_tokens\\": int,\\n        \\"output_tokens\\": int,\\n        \\"total_tokens\\": int\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### TR3: Model Pricing\\nCurrent Claude pricing (January 2024):\\n- **Claude 3.5 Sonnet**: $3/million input, $15/million output\\n- **Claude 3 Opus**: $15/million input, $75/million output\\n- **Claude 3 Haiku**: $0.25/million input, $1.25/million output\\n\\n### TR4: Frontend Components\\n- **TR4.1**: Update `AgentSummaryPane.jsx` with new display elements\\n- **TR4.2**: Implement formatting utilities for cost/duration\\n- **TR4.3**: Add appropriate icons/styling for metrics\\n- **TR4.4**: Ensure responsive layout\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n### US1: Cost Visibility\\n**As a** user running AI workflows  \\n**I want to** see the cost of each agent execution  \\n**So that** I can understand and optimize my AI spending\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Cost displayed as badge in agent summary (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n- Cost calculated from actual token usage when available\\n- Cost appears when agent completes\\n- Cost shows appropriate precision (4 decimal places for small amounts)\\n\\n### US2: Performance Monitoring\\n**As a** user debugging workflows  \\n**I want to** see how long each agent takes to execute  \\n**So that** I can identify performance bottlenecks\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Duration displayed as badge in agent summary (e.g., \\"2.3s\\")\\n- Duration shows from agent start to completion\\n- Duration formatted appropriately (ms for <1s, s for <1min, m s for longer)\\n- Start/completion times visible in summary\\n\\n### US3: Model Transparency\\n**As a** user optimizing workflows  \\n**I want to** see which AI model each agent used  \\n**So that** I can understand model selection and costs\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Model displayed as tag in agent summary (e.g., \\"Sonnet 3.5\\")\\n- Model name shortened for readability\\n- Model associated with specific agent execution\\n- Model information persists after completion\\n\\n### US4: Real-time Updates\\n**As a** user monitoring live workflows  \\n**I want to** see metrics appear as agents complete  \\n**So that** I can track progress and costs in real-time\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Start time appears when agent begins\\n- Metrics appear when agent completes\\n- UI updates via WebSocket without page refresh\\n- No visible delays in metric display\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- **TC1**: Must not impact agent execution performance\\n- **TC2**: Must maintain backward compatibility with existing API consumers\\n- **TC3**: Must handle network failures gracefully during metric collection\\n- **TC4**: Must use existing authentication and authorization mechanisms\\n\\n### Business Constraints\\n- **BC1**: Model pricing hardcoded initially (updatable in future)\\n- **BC2**: No budget controls or alerting in initial version\\n- **BC3**: No historical analytics or cost aggregation\\n- **BC4**: Focus on individual agent metrics only\\n\\n### Technology Constraints\\n- **TK1**: Use existing Python backend and React frontend\\n- **TK2**: Leverage existing activity tracking infrastructure\\n- **TK3**: Follow existing UI design patterns and styling\\n- **TK4**: Use Claude API token usage data as primary source\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n### User Acceptance\\n1. **Cost Visibility**: Users can see cost for 95% of completed agents\\n2. **Duration Accuracy**: Duration displayed within 100ms of actual execution time\\n3. **Model Information**: Model name visible for all agents\\n4. **Performance Impact**: < 5% overhead added to agent execution time\\n5. **UI Responsiveness**: Metrics appear within 1 second of agent completion\\n\\n### Technical Acceptance\\n1. **API Compatibility**: Existing API consumers continue working without changes\\n2. **Error Handling**: System gracefully handles missing or invalid metric data\\n3. **Test Coverage**: 90% test coverage for new components\\n4. **Documentation**: All new APIs and components documented\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n### Current Version\\n- **Historical cost analytics and reporting**\\n- **Budget controls and alerting**\\n- **Cost breakdown by tool or iteration**\\n- **Real-time streaming cost updates during execution**\\n- **Cost aggregation across multiple agents**\\n- **External cost tracking integrations**\\n- **Cost optimization recommendations**\\n\\n### Future Considerations\\n- Integration with external budget tracking systems\\n- Advanced cost analytics and visualizations\\n- Predictive cost modeling\\n- Multi-cloud cost tracking\\n- Cost alerts and budget controls\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n### Technical Assumptions\\n- Claude API responses include `usage` field with token counts\\n- Activity tracker can be extended without breaking existing functionality\\n- WebSocket connections remain stable for real-time updates\\n- Agent runtime provides access to model configuration\\n\\n### Business Assumptions\\n- Current model pricing remains stable during implementation\\n- Users primarily interested in per-agent costs vs. aggregate costs\\n- Cost precision to 4 decimal places sufficient for user needs\\n- Duration tracking in milliseconds adequate for performance analysis\\n\\n### User Assumptions\\n- Users understand AI model cost concepts\\n- Users can interpret duration and cost metrics effectively\\n- Users will use cost information for workflow optimization\\n- Users prioritize accuracy over real-time streaming updates\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n### Internal Dependencies\\n- Activity Tracker system (`activity_tracker.py`)\\n- Agent Runtime system\\n- WebSocket/API infrastructure (`main.py`)\\n- AgentSummaryPane component\\n- Existing authentication/authorization\\n\\n### External Dependencies\\n- Claude API with consistent token usage reporting\\n- React framework for frontend updates\\n- Python 3.11+ for backend enhancements\\n- Existing build and deployment pipeline\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n### Development Methodology\\n- **Test-Driven Development (TDD)**: Write tests first, then implementation\\n- **Incremental Delivery**: Backend \\u2192 API \\u2192 Frontend phases\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Ensure existing functionality unaffected\\n- **Performance Monitoring**: Track impact on execution speed\\n\\n### Testing Strategy\\n1. **Unit Tests**: Cost calculation, formatting utilities, data structures\\n2. **Integration Tests**: End-to-end flow from agent execution to UI display\\n3. **API Tests**: Response format validation and backward compatibility\\n4. **Frontend Tests**: Component rendering and data handling\\n5. **Performance Tests**: Execution overhead measurement\\n\\n### Risk Mitigation\\n- **Missing Token Data**: Fallback to estimation based on character counts\\n- **API Changes**: Defensive programming for token usage field changes\\n- **Performance Impact**: Asynchronous processing where possible\\n- **UI Compatibility**: Progressive enhancement with feature detection\\n\\nThis requirements document provides the foundation for implementing agent cost tracking enhancement using test-driven development methodology."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 81.5%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not